const VINE_EDU_READING={
  'data structures & algorithms':{title:'Data Structures & Algorithms',lead:'A practical guide to choosing data structures, reasoning about complexity, and building correct algorithms.',sections:[['1. Big O and growth rates','Big O describes how an algorithm scales as input size n grows. O(1) is constant, O(log n) grows slowly, O(n) scans the input, and O(n log n) is common for efficient sorting. Ignore constants when comparing growth: 3n + 8 is O(n). Always state what n represents and consider auxiliary space as well as time.','Example: two nested loops over n items usually take O(n²); one pass to find a maximum takes O(n).'],['2. Arrays, stacks and queues','Arrays store elements in indexed, contiguous positions: access is O(1), while inserting at the front usually shifts elements and costs O(n). A stack is last-in, first-out and supports push/pop; it is useful for undo, parsing and depth-first search. A queue is first-in, first-out and is useful for scheduling and breadth-first search.','When implementing a queue with an array, use a circular buffer or deque to avoid shifting every item after removal.'],['3. Trees and graphs','A tree is a connected graph without cycles. Binary search trees support ordered search in O(h), where h is tree height; balancing keeps h near log n. Graphs model networks using adjacency lists (space O(V+E)) or matrices (space O(V²)). BFS explores by distance; DFS explores a path deeply.','Use BFS for shortest paths in an unweighted graph. Use a visited set to avoid revisiting nodes and looping on cycles.'],['4. Sorting and searching','Binary search needs sorted data and halves the search range each step, giving O(log n) time. Merge sort guarantees O(n log n) time and uses extra memory; quicksort is typically O(n log n) but can degrade to O(n²) with poor pivots. Choose based on stability, memory and input constraints.','Binary search invariant: if the target is present, it remains inside the current inclusive interval [left, right].'],['5. Recursion and dynamic programming','Recursion solves a problem using smaller instances. Every recursive function needs a base case and progress toward it. Dynamic programming stores answers to overlapping subproblems: memoization caches recursive results, while tabulation fills a table iteratively.','For Fibonacci, naive recursion repeats work exponentially. Storing earlier values reduces the computation to O(n) time and O(n) space.']],quiz:[['Which complexity describes a single full scan?',['O(1)','O(log n)','O(n)','O(n²)'],2,'A scan visits each element once, so work grows linearly.'],['Which structure is last-in, first-out?',['Queue','Stack','Heap','Graph'],1,'A stack removes the most recently added item first.'],['Which search finds shortest paths in an unweighted graph?',['DFS','BFS','Binary search','Quicksort'],1,'BFS explores vertices in increasing number of edges from the start.'],['What prerequisite does binary search need?',['Random values','Sorted data','A tree','Constant memory'],1,'Sorted order lets each comparison discard half the remaining range.'],['What makes dynamic programming useful?',['No repeated work','Overlapping subproblems','Only sorted input','No base cases'],1,'Caching overlapping subproblems avoids recomputing the same answers.']]},
  'engineering mathematics':{title:'Engineering Mathematics II',lead:'Core tools for modelling change, signals, and multivariable engineering systems.',sections:[['1. Differential equations','A differential equation relates a function to its derivatives. For a first-order linear equation y′ + P(x)y = Q(x), an integrating factor μ = e^(∫P dx) turns the left side into (μy)′. Apply initial conditions after finding the general solution.','Example: for y′ + 2y = 0, separation gives y = Ce^(−2x); an initial value determines C.'],['2. Laplace transforms','The Laplace transform maps a time function to a complex-frequency function: L{f(t)} = F(s). It turns derivatives into algebraic expressions, which helps solve initial-value problems and analyse circuits. For f′, L{f′}=sF(s)−f(0).','Keep initial conditions in the transformed equation; dropping them changes the physical response.'],['3. Fourier series','Periodic signals can be represented as sums of sines and cosines. Fourier coefficients measure how much of each frequency is present. Symmetry can simplify the work: even functions use cosine terms, odd functions use sine terms.','More terms improve approximation away from discontinuities, but oscillations near a jump persist (Gibbs phenomenon).'],['4. Partial derivatives and gradients','For a function of several variables, a partial derivative changes one variable while holding the others fixed. The gradient points toward greatest increase. The total differential estimates small output changes: df ≈ fx dx + fy dy.','In optimisation, an interior stationary point has zero gradient; use second derivatives or the Hessian to classify it.'],['5. Multiple integrals','Double integrals accumulate a quantity over a region. Choose integration order and bounds that match the geometry. In polar coordinates, dA = r dr dθ. Change of variables requires the Jacobian determinant.','Sketch the region before setting bounds; reversed limits are a frequent source of errors.']],quiz:[['The integrating factor for y′+2y=0 is:',['e^x','e^(2x)','2x','ln x'],1,'μ=e^(∫2dx)=e^(2x).'],['Laplace transform of f′ includes which initial term?',['+f(0)','−f(0)','+f′(0)','−s f(0)'],1,'L{f′}=sF(s)−f(0).'],['An odd periodic function has which Fourier terms?',['Cosines only','Sines only','Constant only','No harmonics'],1,'Odd symmetry cancels the constant and cosine coefficients.'],['The gradient points toward:',['Fastest increase','Fastest decrease','Zero curvature','Smallest input'],0,'The gradient gives the direction of steepest local increase.'],['Polar area element is:',['dr dθ','r dr dθ','r² dr dθ','2πr dr'],1,'The Jacobian contributes the factor r.']]},
  'machine learning':{title:'Machine Learning',lead:'A foundation in data, models, evaluation, and responsible deployment.',sections:[['1. Learning setup','Supervised learning uses labelled examples. Regression predicts continuous values; classification predicts categories. Unsupervised learning finds structure without target labels. Split data into training, validation and test sets before tuning.','Keep related records in the same split when leakage is possible, such as multiple measurements from one person.'],['2. Features and preprocessing','Features encode useful information for a model. Handle missing values deliberately, encode categories, and scale numeric inputs when the algorithm depends on distance or gradient size. Fit preprocessing only on training data, then apply the same transform to validation/test data.','Data leakage occurs when information unavailable at prediction time enters training or preprocessing.'],['3. Models and overfitting','A model that memorises training examples but performs poorly on new data is overfit. Regularisation penalises complexity; cross-validation estimates generalisation across several splits. Begin with a simple baseline before trying a complex model.','A large train–validation performance gap is a warning to inspect leakage, model complexity, and dataset size.'],['4. Metrics','Accuracy can hide poor performance on imbalanced classes. Precision asks what fraction of positive predictions were correct; recall asks what fraction of actual positives were found. F1 balances precision and recall. Use MAE/RMSE for regression depending on error costs.','Choose metrics from the real cost of mistakes, not because one score is familiar.'],['5. Responsible deployment','Monitor data drift and model quality after release. Document intended use, limitations, and failure cases; protect sensitive data and provide human review for high-impact decisions.','A model is part of a system: data collection, interfaces, monitoring and recourse affect outcomes too.']],quiz:[['Regression predicts:',['A continuous value','Only clusters','A graph path','A password'],0,'Regression estimates numeric quantities.'],['When should preprocessing be fitted?',['On all data','On training data only','On test data','After deployment'],1,'Fit transforms on training data to avoid leakage.'],['Overfitting means:',['Poor train and test scores','Good training but weak generalisation','No features','Too little data always'],1,'The model has learned training-specific patterns that do not generalise.'],['Recall measures:',['Correct positives among predicted positives','Found positives among all actual positives','Overall correct predictions','Average squared error'],1,'Recall = true positives / (true positives + false negatives).'],['Why monitor a deployed model?',['Data and performance can change','Models never change','To avoid testing','To increase training labels'],0,'Real-world data distributions and outcomes can drift over time.']]},
  'artificial intelligence':{title:'Artificial Intelligence',lead:'Search, reasoning, planning, and modern AI systems—with attention to limits and safety.',sections:[['1. Agents and environments','An agent observes an environment and selects actions to reach a goal. A rational agent chooses actions that maximise expected performance given its information. Environments differ in observability, uncertainty, dynamics and number of agents.','A route planner needs a state representation, legal actions, a goal test and a cost function.'],['2. Search','Breadth-first search finds shallowest paths when step costs are equal. Uniform-cost search handles different non-negative costs. A* uses f(n)=g(n)+h(n), combining cost so far and an estimate to the goal. An admissible heuristic never overestimates remaining cost.','A* is optimal with an admissible heuristic under the usual non-negative path-cost assumptions.'],['3. Knowledge and logic','Propositional logic represents facts and connectives. First-order logic adds objects, relations and quantifiers. Inference derives conclusions from a knowledge base, but conclusions depend on the correctness and completeness of the represented facts.','A useful knowledge representation makes important assumptions explicit and keeps facts separate from inference rules.'],['4. Machine learning within AI','Learning systems infer patterns from data, while search and planning can operate from explicit rules or models. Neural networks can represent complex functions but need careful data, validation and evaluation. Generative systems can produce plausible errors.','Treat generated text as a proposal to verify, especially for calculations, citations and safety-critical advice.'],['5. Evaluation and safety','Define success before deployment. Evaluate robustness, bias, privacy, security and failure recovery; test realistic edge cases. Keep people able to understand uncertainty and contest consequential outcomes.','A benchmark score alone does not establish that a system is reliable in a different setting.']],quiz:[['An AI agent maps observations to:',['Actions','Only labels','Database rows','Gradients'],0,'An agent selects actions based on observations and its policy.'],['Which search handles unequal non-negative path costs?',['BFS','Uniform-cost search','DFS','Hill climbing'],1,'Uniform-cost expands the lowest accumulated-cost path.'],['A* evaluation is:',['g+h','g−h','h/g','g×h'],0,'g is cost so far and h estimates cost remaining.'],['An admissible heuristic:',['Never overestimates','Always equals true cost','Is negative','Ignores the goal'],0,'It is optimistic, preserving optimality under standard assumptions.'],['Why verify generated answers?',['They can sound plausible while wrong','They are always encrypted','They cannot use data','They are deterministic'],0,'Generative output is not guaranteed to be factually correct.']]},
  'digital electronics':{title:'Digital Electronics',lead:'Understand binary logic, combinational circuits, sequential systems and timing.',sections:[['1. Number systems','Digital circuits represent information with binary digits. Convert a binary number to decimal by summing each bit times its power of two. Two’s complement represents signed integers; invert the bits and add one to negate a value.','For n-bit two’s complement, the representable range is −2^(n−1) to 2^(n−1)−1.'],['2. Boolean logic','AND, OR and NOT form basic logic operations. De Morgan’s laws convert between forms: NOT(A AND B)=NOT A OR NOT B. Truth tables make behaviour explicit; Boolean algebra and Karnaugh maps simplify logic.','Simpler logic can reduce gate count, delay, area and power, but verify the result against the original truth table.'],['3. Combinational circuits','Outputs depend only on current inputs. Adders, multiplexers, decoders and comparators are common building blocks. A multiplexer selects one input using select bits.','A full adder produces sum A⊕B⊕Cin and carry AB + ACin + BCin.'],['4. Sequential circuits','Sequential circuits store state. Latches are level-sensitive; flip-flops sample at a clock edge. Registers hold groups of bits and finite-state machines transition between defined states.','A synchronous design needs a clear clock and reset strategy, with state transitions defined for every relevant input.'],['5. Timing and hazards','Setup time is the interval data must be stable before a clock edge; hold time is the interval it remains stable afterward. Propagation delay limits clock frequency. Glitches can occur when paths have different delays.','Check worst-case path delay and timing constraints; a logically correct circuit can still fail timing.']],quiz:[['Binary 1010 equals decimal:',['8','9','10','12'],2,'1010₂ = 8+2 = 10.'],['Two’s complement negation is formed by:',['Invert and add one','Add two','Shift left','Clear the sign bit'],0,'Invert all bits, then add one.'],['A multiplexer:',['Selects one input','Stores a bit','Adds two numbers','Generates a clock'],0,'Select lines choose which input reaches the output.'],['A flip-flop is generally:',['Edge-triggered','Always combinational','A decoder','An analogue filter'],0,'Flip-flops sample state at a clock edge.'],['Setup time is required:',['Before the clock edge','After reset only','Between two outputs','During power off'],0,'Input data must be stable for setup time before sampling.']]},
  'materials science':{title:'Materials Science',lead:'Connect material structure to properties, processing, and engineering selection.',sections:[['1. Atomic structure and bonding','Material behaviour starts with atoms and bonds. Metallic bonding supports electrical conductivity and ductility; covalent bonds are directional and can be strong; ionic solids often resist deformation but may be brittle. Crystal structure describes repeating atomic arrangements.','Bonding helps explain trends, but defects and microstructure also strongly affect real properties.'],['2. Crystal defects','Vacancies, dislocations and grain boundaries are defects. Dislocation motion enables plastic deformation. Grain boundaries can impede dislocations, often increasing strength as grain size decreases (Hall–Petch trend) within its applicable range.','Cold working raises dislocation density and strength, while annealing can restore ductility through recovery and recrystallisation.'],['3. Mechanical properties','Stress is force per area; strain is relative deformation. In the elastic region, σ=Eε, where E is Young’s modulus. Yield strength marks the start of significant permanent deformation; toughness is energy absorbed before fracture.','A stiff material is not automatically strong or tough. Select properties against the actual load and failure mode.'],['4. Phase diagrams and heat treatment','Phase diagrams show stable phases versus temperature and composition at equilibrium. Heat treatment changes microstructure by controlling heating and cooling. A lever rule can estimate phase fractions in a two-phase region.','Real processing may not reach equilibrium; cooling rate can produce metastable structures.'],['5. Corrosion and selection','Corrosion is material degradation through chemical or electrochemical reactions. Selection considers strength, weight, temperature, environment, manufacturability, cost and lifecycle. Protective coatings and design that avoids crevices can reduce corrosion risk.','Use a material selection chart as a filter, then validate with environment-specific testing.']],quiz:[['Young’s modulus relates:',['Stress and elastic strain','Mass and volume','Heat and pressure','Voltage and current'],0,'In the linear elastic range, σ=Eε.'],['Plastic deformation is:',['Permanent','Always reversible','Only thermal','A crystal phase'],0,'Plastic strain remains after unloading.'],['Dislocations primarily enable:',['Plastic deformation','Electrical insulation','Evaporation','Magnetism only'],0,'Their motion allows slip at stresses below ideal crystal strength.'],['Corrosion protection can include:',['Protective coatings','More crevices','Removing all inspection','Increasing moisture'],0,'Coatings separate the material from the corrosive environment.'],['Material selection should consider:',['Only strength','Load, environment and lifecycle','Only colour','Only density'],1,'Engineering selection balances performance, process, environment and cost.']]}
};
function vineduQuizHistoryRows(course){
  const records=(Array.isArray(db.quizAttempts)?db.quizAttempts:[]).filter(item=>item.course===course).slice().reverse();
  if(!records.length)return '<p class="study-history-empty">No attempts yet. Your completed quizzes will appear here.</p>';
  return `<ol>${records.map(item=>`<li><b>${Number(item.score)||0}/5 · ${Number(item.percent)||0}%</b><span>${Number(item.percent)>=80?'Strong understanding':Number(item.percent)>=60?'Good progress':'Keep practising'}</span><time>${item.at?new Date(item.at).toLocaleString():''}</time></li>`).join('')}</ol>`
}
const VINE_EDU_DSA_LESSONS={
 'big o analysis':{intro:'Big O gives a machine-independent way to describe how resource use grows as an input grows. It helps compare approaches before implementation details or hardware obscure the difference.',parts:[['1. Count growth, not seconds','Let n describe the input size. A loop that visits n values performs work proportional to n, or O(n). Two nested loops that each visit n values perform about n² operations, or O(n²). A loop that halves its remaining range at every step takes O(log n). When expressions are simplified, constants and lower-order terms are dropped: 4n² + 3n + 20 is O(n²). This is an asymptotic upper bound, not an exact stopwatch prediction.'],['2. Common complexity classes','O(1): direct array access or swapping two values. O(log n): binary search in sorted input. O(n): finding a maximum in an unsorted list. O(n log n): merge sort and typical efficient comparison sorting. O(n²): comparing every pair with two full loops. O(2ⁿ): trying every subset, which quickly becomes impractical. The difference becomes dramatic at large n: doubling n roughly doubles linear work, but multiplies quadratic work by four.'],['3. Time and auxiliary space','Time complexity counts operations as input grows. Auxiliary space counts extra memory beyond the input. Iterative maximum-finding takes O(n) time and O(1) extra space. Merge sort takes O(n log n) time and typically O(n) extra space. A recursive algorithm also uses a call stack: recursion depth n can consume O(n) stack space. State which resource you are analysing; “complexity is O(n)” is incomplete without saying time or space.'],['4. Best, average and worst cases','Linear search is O(1) in its best case when the first item matches, but O(n) in the worst case when the match is last or absent. Worst-case analysis gives a useful guarantee. Average-case analysis depends on assumptions about input distribution. Amortized analysis averages a sequence of operations: a dynamic array append is usually O(1), although an occasional resize copies n elements. Across many appends, the average cost per append remains O(1).'],['Worked example: choose a search','Suppose a list has one million records. Linear search may inspect one million values. If the data is sorted, binary search needs about log₂(1,000,000), roughly 20 comparisons. But sorting an unsorted list first also costs time. If only one query is needed, sorting may not help; for thousands of queries, the initial sort can pay off. Always include preprocessing and repeated use in the analysis.'],['Self-check','For i from 0 to n−1, compare each item with every later item. There are about n(n−1)/2 comparisons, so the running time is O(n²). Replacing the inner loop with a pointer that only moves forward may reduce the total work to O(n), provided the problem’s ordering invariant allows it.']]},
 'arrays, stacks & queues':{intro:'Arrays, stacks and queues are foundational ways to organise data. Their operation costs explain why one representation fits a task better than another.',parts:[['1. Arrays and dynamic arrays','An array stores elements in indexed positions. Access by index is O(1), because the address can be calculated directly. Searching an unsorted array is O(n). Inserting at the front or middle can require shifting many items, also O(n). A dynamic array reserves extra capacity; when full, it allocates a larger block and copies values. That resize is expensive once, but append is amortized O(1) over a long sequence.'],['2. Stacks: last in, first out','A stack (LIFO) exposes the newest item first. Its core operations are push, pop and peek, usually O(1). The browser Back button can use a stack of visited pages; undo systems keep previous actions on a stack; a compiler uses a stack to track nested parentheses and function calls. To validate brackets, push each opening bracket. At a closing bracket, the top must be its matching opener. A mismatch or leftover opener means the expression is invalid.'],['3. Queues: first in, first out','A queue (FIFO) serves the oldest waiting item first. Enqueue adds at the rear and dequeue removes from the front. Queues model print jobs, customer service and task scheduling. Breadth-first search uses a queue to visit graph nodes in increasing distance from the start. Removing index zero from a plain array may shift every remaining item; a linked queue or circular buffer avoids this repeated O(n) work.'],['4. Deque and priority queue','A deque supports insertion and removal at both ends, useful for sliding-window algorithms. A priority queue returns the highest- or lowest-priority item rather than the oldest. A binary heap implements insertion and removal in O(log n), with peek at O(1). Use FIFO when arrival order matters; use a priority queue when urgency or cost determines the next item.'],['Worked example: bracket checker','Read characters from left to right. Ignore non-bracket characters. Push `(`, `[`, `{` onto a stack. For `)`, `]`, `}`, first ensure the stack is non-empty, then pop and compare the pair. At the end, the stack must be empty. Each character is processed once, so time is O(n), and in the worst case the stack uses O(n) space.'],['Self-check','A clinic serves patients by arrival except for emergencies. A basic queue handles ordinary patients, but emergencies require a priority rule. This is a priority-queue problem, or two queues with an explicit policy. Picking a structure from the required ordering is more important than picking the one with the most familiar name.']]},
 'trees & graphs':{intro:'Trees and graphs describe hierarchical data and networks. Traversal algorithms turn their relationships into systematic, measurable searches.',parts:[['1. Tree vocabulary','A tree is a connected graph with no cycles. The root is the starting node; children descend from a parent; leaves have no children. Height is the longest downward path. A binary search tree orders keys so smaller values lie left and larger values lie right. Search takes O(h), where h is height. A balanced tree has height near log₂ n; an unbalanced tree can become a chain with height n.'],['2. Traversal patterns','Depth-first traversal explores a branch before returning. Preorder visits node, left, right; inorder visits left, node, right; postorder visits children before the node. In a binary search tree, inorder traversal yields sorted order. Breadth-first traversal visits level by level with a queue and is useful for finding the closest node by edge count. Recursive DFS is concise, but very deep structures may exceed the call stack.'],['3. Graph representations','A graph has vertices V and edges E. An adjacency list stores each vertex’s neighbours and uses O(V+E) space, making it efficient for sparse graphs. An adjacency matrix uses O(V²) space but checks whether an edge exists in O(1), useful for dense graphs. Edges may be directed or undirected and may carry weights such as distance, time or cost.'],['4. BFS and DFS','BFS uses a queue and visits each vertex and edge at most a constant number of times, giving O(V+E) with an adjacency list. In an unweighted graph, BFS finds shortest paths by number of edges. DFS uses recursion or a stack; it supports cycle detection, connected components and topological reasoning. Mark a vertex visited when adding it to the worklist, not only when removing it, to prevent duplicate enqueues.'],['Worked example: campus route','Model buildings as vertices and walkways as edges. To find the route with the fewest walkways, run BFS from the starting building. Store each newly discovered vertex’s parent. When the destination is reached, follow parent links backward, then reverse that sequence. If walkways have different travel times, ordinary BFS is no longer enough; use Dijkstra’s algorithm for non-negative weights.'],['Self-check','A social network is often sparse: each person connects to a small fraction of all users. An adjacency list usually saves substantial memory. A visited set prevents an undirected edge from sending DFS back and forth forever.']]},
 'sorting and searching':{intro:'Sorting makes data easier to query and analyse. Search algorithms are correct only when their assumptions about ordering and invariants are respected.',parts:[['1. Linear and binary search','Linear search checks elements one by one and works on unsorted data in O(n). Binary search requires sorted data. Keep an interval [low, high]; inspect its midpoint; discard the half that cannot contain the target. The interval shrinks by half each step, giving O(log n) time and O(1) iterative space. Compute midpoint as low + (high−low)//2 to avoid overflow in fixed-width languages.'],['2. Sorting by comparison','Insertion sort grows a sorted prefix by inserting each next value in place. It is O(n²) in general but performs well on small or nearly sorted inputs. Merge sort divides, sorts and merges; it guarantees O(n log n) time and typically needs O(n) extra space. Quicksort partitions around a pivot and is often fast in practice, but poor pivots can cause O(n²) worst-case behaviour.'],['3. Stability and in-place sorting','A stable sort preserves the original order of equal-key items. This matters when sorting records by multiple fields in stages. In-place algorithms use little extra memory, although the precise definition varies. Choose based on input size, memory limits, stability needs and worst-case guarantees—not only average speed.'],['4. Correct binary-search boundaries','With an inclusive interval, use while low <= high. If the midpoint is too small, set low = mid + 1; if too large, set high = mid − 1. For the first position where a condition becomes true, use a lower-bound variant and maintain a different invariant. Many “off-by-one” bugs come from mixing inclusive and half-open intervals.'],['Worked example: lower bound','Given sorted values [2, 4, 4, 4, 9], find the first index whose value is at least 4. Maintain a half-open range [low, high). When a[mid] >= 4, keep the midpoint as a possible answer by moving high = mid; otherwise move low = mid + 1. The result is index 1. This variant also returns the insertion point when the value is absent.'],['Self-check','If you must search once in an unsorted list, linear search is often simplest. If you will search repeatedly, sorting once and then using binary search may be faster overall. Include both the preprocessing cost and number of queries in the comparison.']]},
 'recursion & dynamic programming':{intro:'Recursion expresses a problem through smaller instances. Dynamic programming makes that approach efficient when subproblems overlap.',parts:[['1. Build a correct recursive definition','Every recursive algorithm needs a base case and a step that moves toward it. For factorial, factorial(0)=1 and factorial(n)=n×factorial(n−1) for n>0. If a call does not reduce the problem, recursion may never end. Trace a tiny input by hand and check that each call returns the right partial result.'],['2. Call stack and cost','Each recursive call stores arguments, local variables and a return location. A chain of n calls uses O(n) stack space. A divide-and-conquer algorithm may have logarithmic depth, as in balanced binary search. Recursion is not inherently slower, but repeated work and deep stacks can matter. An iterative version can often replace tail recursion with a loop.'],['3. Overlapping subproblems','Naive Fibonacci recursion computes the same values repeatedly: fib(5) calls fib(4) and fib(3), while fib(4) also calls fib(3). The call tree grows exponentially. Memoization stores each answer the first time it is computed; every later request reuses it. This reduces Fibonacci to O(n) time and O(n) memory.'],['4. Memoization and tabulation','Memoization is top-down: start from the requested result and cache subproblems. Tabulation is bottom-up: fill a table from smallest cases upward. Both exploit overlapping subproblems. A useful DP design states (1) the state, (2) the recurrence, (3) base cases, and (4) evaluation order. For knapsack, a state can be the best value using the first i items with capacity w.'],['Worked example: climbing stairs','If each move climbs one or two steps, ways(n)=ways(n−1)+ways(n−2), with ways(0)=1 and ways(1)=1. A table computes values from 0 to n in O(n) time. Only the last two values are needed, so memory can be reduced to O(1). Always test small cases: n=0 gives one empty way; n=2 gives two ways.'],['Self-check','Before writing code, draw the dependency graph between states. If each state depends only on earlier states, choose an order that computes those first. If the recurrence does not overlap subproblems, dynamic programming may add complexity without saving work.']]}
};
function vineduEnrichLessonDialogs(){const dialogs=document.querySelectorAll('[role="dialog"],dialog,.modal,[class*=modal]');for(const dialog of dialogs){if(dialog.querySelector('.vinedu-long-lesson'))continue;const heading=dialog.querySelector('h1,h2,h3,h4');if(!heading)continue;const topic=heading.textContent.trim().toLowerCase();const key=Object.keys(VINE_EDU_DSA_LESSONS).find(value=>topic.includes(value));if(!key)continue;const content=VINE_EDU_DSA_LESSONS[key];const article=document.createElement('section');article.className='vinedu-long-lesson';article.innerHTML=`<p class="lesson-intro">${content.intro}</p>${content.parts.map(([title,text])=>`<section><h3>${title}</h3><p>${text}</p></section>`).join('')}<p class="lesson-takeaway"><b>Study tip:</b> Explain the key idea in your own words, then solve a small example without looking at the notes.</p>`;const complete=[...dialog.querySelectorAll('button')].find(button=>/mark lesson complete/i.test(button.textContent));if(complete)complete.before(article);else dialog.appendChild(article);dialog.classList.add('vinedu-long-lesson-dialog')}}
function vineduWatchLessons(){if(!document.body)return;vineduEnrichLessonDialogs();new MutationObserver(()=>vineduEnrichLessonDialogs()).observe(document.body,{childList:true,subtree:true})}
if(document.readyState==='loading')document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',vineduWatchLessons,{once:true});else vineduWatchLessons();
function vineduRenderReading(courseKey){
  const key=Object.keys(VINE_EDU_READING).find(k=>courseKey.toLowerCase().includes(k));
  const book=VINE_EDU_READING[key];if(!book)return false;
  const room=[...document.querySelectorAll('h1,h2,h3,h4')].find(h=>/your reading room/i.test(h.textContent))?.closest('[data-reading-room],.reading-room,.reading-room-card,section,article')||[...document.querySelectorAll('h1,h2,h3,h4')].find(h=>/your reading room/i.test(h.textContent))?.parentElement;
  const target=room||document.querySelector('[data-reading-room]');if(!target)return false;
  const body=target.querySelector('.reading-content,[data-reading-content]')||target;
  body.innerHTML=`<div class="vinedu-study"><div class="study-head"><div><div class="study-kicker">COURSE STUDY NOTES · READ & PRACTISE</div><h2>${book.title}</h2></div><button type="button" class="study-print" onclick="window.print()">Download / print PDF</button></div><p class="study-lead">${book.lead}</p><div class="study-progress"><span id="study-progress-label">Reading notes · 0/${book.sections.length}</span><span class="study-track"><i id="study-progress-fill"></i></span></div><nav class="study-toc" aria-label="Course topics">${book.sections.map((s,i)=>`<a href="#study-${i}">${i+1}. ${s[0].replace(/^\d+\. /,'')}</a>`).join('')}</nav>${book.sections.map((s,i)=>`<article class="study-chapter" id="study-${i}"><h3>${s[0]}</h3><p>${s[1]}</p><p class="study-example"><b>Engineering connection</b><br>${s[2]}</p><button type="button" class="study-done" data-study-done="${i}">Mark section read</button></article>`).join('')}<section class="study-quiz"><h3>5-question knowledge check</h3><p>Try the quiz after reading. Your score and explanations will be saved to your learning record.</p><form id="vinedu-book-quiz">${book.quiz.map((q,i)=>`<fieldset><legend>${i+1}. ${q[0]}</legend>${q[1].map((a,j)=>`<label class="study-option"><input type="radio" name="q${i}" value="${j}" required><span>${a}</span></label>`).join('')}</fieldset>`).join('')}<button class="study-submit" type="submit">Submit 5-question quiz</button></form><div id="study-result" aria-live="polite"></div></section></div>`;
  target.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<section class="study-history"><h3>Your quiz history</h3><p>Previous attempts for ${book.title}</p><div class="study-history-list">${vineduQuizHistoryRows(book.title)}</div></section>`);
  let read=new Set();target.onclick=function(e){const b=e.target.closest('[data-study-done]');if(!b)return;read.add(Number(b.dataset.studyDone));b.textContent='✓ Section read';b.disabled=true;target.querySelector('#study-progress-label').textContent=`Reading notes · ${read.size}/${book.sections.length}`;target.querySelector('#study-progress-fill').style.width=`${Math.round(read.size/book.sections.length*100)}%`};
  target.querySelector('#vinedu-book-quiz').addEventListener('submit',function(e){e.preventDefault();let score=0;const feedback=book.quiz.map((q,i)=>{const answer=new FormData(e.currentTarget).get(`q${i}`);const selected=answer===null?-1:Number(answer);const correct=selected===q[2];if(correct)score++;return `<li class="${correct?'correct':'incorrect'}"><b>${correct?'Correct':'Review'} · ${q[0]}</b><br>${q[3]} Correct answer: ${q[1][q[2]]}.</li>`}).join('');const percent=Math.round(score/5*100);const level=percent>=80?'Strong understanding':percent>=60?'Good progress — review missed ideas':'Keep practising — revisit the notes';target.querySelector('#study-result').innerHTML=`<div class="study-score"><b>${score}/5 · ${percent}%</b><span>${level}</span><ol>${feedback}</ol></div>`;e.currentTarget.querySelectorAll('input,button').forEach(x=>x.disabled=true);const attempts=Array.isArray(db.quizAttempts)?db.quizAttempts:[];attempts.push({course:book.title,score,total:5,percent,at:new Date().toISOString()});db.quizAttempts=attempts.slice(-200);target.querySelector('.study-history-list').innerHTML=vineduQuizHistoryRows(book.title);try{if(typeof save==='function')save()}catch(err){console.error('Could not save quiz attempt',err)}});
  return true;
}
if(!document.getElementById('vinedu-study-style')){const s=document.createElement('style');s.id='vinedu-study-style';s.textContent='.vinedu-study{max-width:900px;margin:20px auto;padding:clamp(20px,4vw,48px);background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2ebe5;border-radius:22px;color:#183b32}.study-kicker{font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#267b60}.study-lead{font-size:18px;color:#5c7169}.study-toc{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin:24px 0}.study-toc a,.study-done{padding:9px 13px;border:1px solid #dce8e0;border-radius:10px;background:#f7faf8;color:#216b54;text-decoration:none}.study-chapter{padding:20px 0;border-top:1px solid #e5ece7;scroll-margin-top:24px}.study-chapter p{line-height:1.8}.study-example{padding:14px;background:#f1f7f2;border-left:3px solid #2b8a67;border-radius:8px}.study-track{display:block;height:8px;background:#e7eee8;border-radius:9px;margin-top:9px}.study-track i{display:block;height:100%;width:0;background:#298765;border-radius:9px;transition:width .2s}.study-quiz{padding:22px;background:#f6f9f6;border-radius:16px}.study-quiz fieldset{border:1px solid #dce7df;border-radius:12px;background:#fff;margin:14px 0;padding:16px}.study-quiz legend{font-weight:700}.study-option{display:flex;gap:10px;padding:8px;cursor:pointer}.study-submit,.study-done{padding:10px 16px;cursor:pointer}.study-submit{border:0;border-radius:10px;background:#247b60;color:white;font-weight:700}.study-score{margin-top:18px;padding:18px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #dce7df;border-radius:12px}.study-score> b{font-size:24px;color:#247b60}.study-score li{padding:8px}.study-score .correct{color:#216b54}.study-score .incorrect{color:#9a5c22}@media(max-width:650px){.vinedu-study{margin:8px;padding:18px;border-radius:14px}.study-lead{font-size:16px}}';document.head.appendChild(s)}
if(!document.getElementById('vinedu-history-style')){const s=document.createElement('style');s.id='vinedu-history-style';s.textContent='.study-history{margin-top:22px;padding:20px;border:1px solid #e0e9e3;border-radius:15px;background:#fff}.study-history>p,.study-history-empty{color:#687d74}.study-history-list ol{list-style:none;padding:0}.study-history-list li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto;gap:4px 14px;padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid #e7eee9}.study-history-list li b{color:#237b60}.study-history-list li span{color:#50665d}.study-history-list time{grid-column:1/-1;font-size:12px;color:#809188}@media(max-width:600px){.study-history-list li{grid-template-columns:1fr}.study-history-list li time{grid-column:auto}}';document.head.appendChild(s)}
document.addEventListener('click',function(e){const control=e.target.closest('button,a');if(!control||!/^read\b/i.test(control.textContent.trim()))return;const row=control.closest('article,li,[class*=resource],[class*=ebook],[class*=book]')||control.parentElement?.parentElement;const title=row?.querySelector('h1,h2,h3,h4,strong,b')?.textContent||row?.innerText||'';if(vineduRenderReading(title)){e.preventDefault();e.stopImmediatePropagation()}},true);
function vineduUpgradeOutline(){const marker=[...document.querySelectorAll('p,div,small')].find(el=>el.children.length===0&&/sample notes are an outline only/i.test(el.textContent||''));if(!marker)return;const region=marker.closest('section,article,[class*=reading],[class*=ebook]')||marker.parentElement?.parentElement||document;const headings=[...region.querySelectorAll('h1,h2,h3,h4,strong,b')].map(el=>el.textContent.trim()).filter(Boolean);const title=headings.find(value=>Object.keys(VINE_EDU_READING).some(key=>value.toLowerCase().includes(key)))||region.innerText;if(vineduRenderReading(title))marker.remove()}
function vineduWatchReader(){if(!document.body)return;vineduUpgradeOutline();new MutationObserver(()=>vineduUpgradeOutline()).observe(document.body,{childList:true,subtree:true})}
if(document.readyState==='loading')document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',vineduWatchReader,{once:true});else vineduWatchReader();
function vineduSetAvatar(src){document.querySelectorAll('[data-profile-avatar],.profile-avatar,.avatar,[class*=avatar]').forEach(node=>{if(node.closest('.study-quiz'))return;node.style.position='relative';node.style.overflow='hidden';node.style.backgroundImage=`url("${src}")`;node.style.backgroundPosition='center';node.style.backgroundSize='cover';node.style.color='transparent';let img=node.querySelector('img[data-vinedu-photo]');if(!img){img=document.createElement('img');img.dataset.vineduPhoto='true';img.alt='Profile photo';img.style.cssText='position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;border-radius:inherit';node.appendChild(img)}img.src=src})}
function vineduRestoreAvatar(){const src=db?.profile?.photo||db?.profile?.avatar||db?.profilePhoto;if(src)vineduSetAvatar(src)}
document.addEventListener('change',event=>{const input=event.target;if(!(input instanceof HTMLInputElement)||input.type!=='file')return;const nearby=(input.closest('section,form,article')?.innerText||'')+' '+(input.getAttribute('aria-label')||'')+' '+(input.accept||'');if(!/photo|avatar|image|profile/i.test(nearby))return;const file=input.files?.[0];if(!file)return;if(!/^image\/(jpeg|png|webp)$/.test(file.type)||file.size>2*1024*1024){alert('Choose a JPEG, PNG or WebP photo under 2 MB.');input.value='';return}const reader=new FileReader();reader.onload=()=>{const src=String(reader.result);db.profile=db.profile||{};db.profile.photo=src;db.profile.avatar=src;db.profilePhoto=src;vineduSetAvatar(src);try{if(typeof save==='function')save()}catch(err){console.error('Could not save profile photo',err)}};reader.readAsDataURL(file)});
if(document.readyState==='loading')document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',vineduRestoreAvatar,{once:true});else vineduRestoreAvatar();
if(!document.getElementById('vinedu-layout-fixes')){const s=document.createElement('style');s.id='vinedu-layout-fixes';s.textContent='aside,.sidebar,[class*=sidebar]{max-height:100vh;max-height:100dvh;overflow-y:auto;overscroll-behavior:contain;scrollbar-gutter:stable} .study-head{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px}.study-print{border:1px solid #dce8e0;background:#f7faf8;color:#216b54;padding:9px 13px;cursor:pointer}.study-chapter p{max-width:78ch}.study-example{line-height:1.7}@media(max-width:620px){.study-head{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}}@media print{body *{visibility:hidden!important}.vinedu-study,.vinedu-study *{visibility:visible!important}.vinedu-study{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;max-width:none;margin:0;padding:0;border:0;box-shadow:none;font:12pt/1.6 Georgia,serif;color:#111}.study-toc,.study-progress,.study-done,.study-quiz,.study-history,.study-print{display:none!important}.study-chapter{break-inside:avoid;border-color:#bbb}.study-example{background:#f4f4f4!important;-webkit-print-color-adjust:exact;print-color-adjust:exact}h2,h3{break-after:avoid}a{color:#111;text-decoration:none}}';document.head.appendChild(s)}
document.addEventListener('keydown',event=>{
  if(event.key==='/'&&!event.ctrlKey&&!event.metaKey&&!event.altKey){
    const target=event.target;
    if(target instanceof HTMLElement&&(/INPUT|TEXTAREA|SELECT/.test(target.tagName)||target.isContentEditable))return;
    const search=[...document.querySelectorAll('input')].find(input=>/search/i.test((input.placeholder||'')+' '+(input.getAttribute('aria-label')||'')));
    if(search){event.preventDefault();search.focus();search.select()}
  }
});
function isCourseStarted(id){return (db.startedCourses||[]).includes(id)}
function pct(c){if(!isCourseStarted(c.id))return 0;const total=Math.max(1,c.topics?.length||1),done=(db.completed||[]).filter(key=>key.startsWith(`${c.id}:`)).length;return Math.round(Math.min(100,done/total*100))}
function esc(v=''){return String(v).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]))}
function icon(c){return c.icon||'📚'}
function go(v){view=v;quizState=null;applyTheme();document.getElementById('app').innerHTML=renderApp();document.querySelectorAll('.nav-btn[data-view]').forEach(x=>x.onclick=()=>go(x.dataset.view));bindView();decorateProfile();applyRolePermissions();decorateCourseProgress();if(view==='Settings')decorateProfileSettings();window.scrollTo(0,0)}
function renderLogin(){return `<main class="login-layout"><div class="login-card"><section class="login-promo"><div class="logo"><div class="logo-mark">V</div><div><div class="logo-name">vinedu</div><div class="logo-sub">ENGINEERING LEARNING</div></div></div><div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow">LEARN WITH CLARITY</div><h1>Your next idea starts here.</h1><p>A personal learning space for engineering students. Learn at your pace, practice with course quizzes and track your progress.</p><ul class="perks"><li><span class="tick">✓</span> Computer science and engineering courses</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span> Your own saved progress and study activity</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span> Separate student and administrator access</li></ul></div><div class="login-footer">VINEDU · ENGINEERING LEARNING SPACE</div></section><section class="login-form"><h2>${authMode==='signup'?'Create your account':'Welcome back'}</h2><div class="login-sub">${authMode==='signup'?'Join Vinedu and start learning engineering.':selectedRole==='admin'?'Administrator sign in to manage your learning space.':'Sign in to continue to your learning space.'}</div><div class="role-switch"><button class="${selectedRole==='student'?'active':''}" data-role="student">Student</button><button class="${selectedRole==='admin'?'active':''}" data-role="admin">Administrator</button></div><div class="tabs"><button class="${authMode==='login'?'active':''}" data-auth="login">Log in</button>${selectedRole==='student'?`<button class="${authMode==='signup'?'active':''}" data-auth="signup">Create account</button>`:''}</div><form id="login-form">${authMode==='signup'?'<label class="field">Your name<input id="user-name" required minlength="2" maxlength="80" autocomplete="name" placeholder="e.g. Alex Morgan"></label>':''}<label class="field">Email address<input id="user-email" required type="email" maxlength="254" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com"></label><label class="field">Password<input id="user-password" required type="password" autocomplete="${authMode==='signup'?'new-password':'current-password'}" placeholder="${authMode==='signup'?'Use at least 12 characters':'Enter your password'}" minlength="${authMode==='signup'?12:1}" maxlength="128"></label><button class="submit-btn" type="submit">${authMode==='signup'?'Create account':'Log in'}</button></form><div class="note"><span>🔒</span><span>Your password is stored as a salted hash. Student and administrator access is checked by the server.</span></div><div class="demo-hint" id="auth-error" role="alert" style="color:#a34141">${esc(window.authError||'')}</div></section></div></main>`}
function startAuth(){const form=document.getElementById('login-form');form.onsubmit=async e=>{e.preventDefault();const submit=form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');submit.disabled=true;submit.textContent=authMode==='signup'?'Creating account…':'Signing in…';const payload={email:document.getElementById('user-email').value.trim(),password:document.getElementById('user-password').value};if(authMode==='signup')payload.name=document.getElementById('user-name').value.trim();else payload.role=selectedRole;try{const r=await fetch(authMode==='signup'?'/api/register':'/api/login',{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},credentials:'same-origin',body:JSON.stringify(payload)}),data=await r.json();if(!r.ok)throw Error(data.error||'Could not sign in.');window.authError='';db=prepareUser(data.user);saveQueue=Promise.resolve();go('Overview')}catch(err){window.authError=err.message;renderLoginPage()} };document.querySelectorAll('[data-role]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{selectedRole=b.dataset.role;authMode='login';window.authError='';renderLoginPage()});document.querySelectorAll('[data-auth]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{authMode=b.dataset.auth;window.authError='';renderLoginPage()})}
function renderLoginPage(){document.getElementById('app').innerHTML=renderLogin();startAuth();if(selectedRole==='admin'&&window.localDemoAdmin){const err=document.getElementById('auth-error');err?.insertAdjacentHTML('beforebegin',`<div class="admin-banner" style="margin-top:16px"><b>Local demo administrator</b><br>Email: ${esc(window.localDemoAdmin.email)}<br>Password: ${esc(window.localDemoAdmin.password)}<br>Local recovery code: ${esc(window.localDemoAdmin.resetToken||'See your local .env file')}</div>`)}if(selectedRole==='admin'){document.querySelector('.login-form')?.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<details class="panel" style="margin-top:16px"><summary style="cursor:pointer;font-weight:700;font-size:12px">Forgot admin password?</summary><form id="admin-password-reset-form"><label class="field">Admin email<input id="reset-admin-email" type="email" required maxlength="254" placeholder="admin@example.com" value="${esc(window.localDemoAdmin?.email||'')}"></label><label class="field">Private reset code<input id="reset-admin-token" type="password" required autocomplete="off" placeholder="Enter your recovery code"></label><label class="field">New password<input id="reset-admin-password" type="password" required minlength="12" maxlength="128" placeholder="At least 12 characters"></label><button class="secondary-btn" style="margin-top:12px">Reset admin password</button></form></details>`)}}
function renderApp(){const admin=db.role==='admin';const nav=admin?[['Overview','⌂'],['Courses','▤'],['Students','♙'],['Assignments','▣'],['Live classes','◉'],['Ebooks','▧'],['AI tutor','✳'],['Analytics','▥'],['Settings','⚙']]:[['Overview','⌂'],['My learning','▤'],['Explore courses','⌕'],['Practice quiz','✓'],['Flashcards','▣'],['Study planner','◷'],['My notes','✎'],['Achievements','✦'],['Career roadmap','↗'],['Assignments','▣'],['Live classes','◉'],['Ebooks','▧'],['AI tutor','✳'],['Analytics','▥'],['Settings','⚙']];return `<div class="shell"><aside class="sidebar"><div class="side-brand"><div class="logo-mark">V</div><div><div class="logo-name">vinedu</div><div class="logo-sub">ENGINEERING LEARNING</div></div></div><div class="side-label">Learning space</div><nav class="nav">${nav.map(([label,ico])=>`<button class="nav-btn ${view===label?'active':''}" data-view="${esc(label)}"><span class="ico">${ico}</span>${esc(label)}</button>`).join('')}</nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><div class="side-label">Account</div><button class="nav-btn" id="logout"><span class="ico">↪</span>Sign out</button><div class="profile-small"><div class="avatar">${esc(db.name[0]?.toUpperCase()||'V')}</div><div class="profile-copy"><b>${esc(db.name)}</b><span>${admin?'Administrator':'Engineering student'}</span></div><button class="icon-button" title="Settings" data-setting="Account">⚙</button></div></div></aside><main class="main"><header class="topbar"><div class="crumb"><button class="icon-button mobile-menu" aria-label="Go to overview" id="home-mobile">⌂</button>Vinedu <span style="color:#b7c0b9">/</span> ${esc(view)}</div><div class="top-actions"><input id="global-search" class="search-input" placeholder="⌕  Search courses…" aria-label="Search courses"><button class="theme-toggle" id="theme-toggle" aria-label="Switch colour theme" title="Switch colour theme">${db.settings?.theme==='dark'?'☀':'☾'}</button><button class="icon-button" id="notif" title="Notifications">♧</button><div class="avatar" style="width:32px;height:32px;font-size:12px">${esc(db.name[0]?.toUpperCase()||'V')}</div></div></header><section class="page">${renderView()}</section></main></div>`}
function progressAverage(){const enrolled=allCourses().filter(c=>(db.enrolled||[]).includes(c.id));return enrolled.length?Math.round(enrolled.reduce((a,c)=>a+pct(c),0)/enrolled.length):0}
function stats(){const activities=db.activity||[], today=new Date().toDateString();const mins=activities.filter(a=>new Date(a.at).toDateString()===today).reduce((s,a)=>s+(a.minutes||1),0);const quizzes=Object.keys(db.attempts||{}).length;return `<div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-top">Enrolled courses<span class="stat-icon">▤</span></div><div class="stat-num">${db.role==='admin'?allCourses().length:(db.enrolled||[]).length}</div><div class="stat-foot">${db.role==='admin'?'Courses in your catalogue':'Your active learning paths'}</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-top">Learning progress<span class="stat-icon">◔</span></div><div class="stat-num">${progressAverage()}%</div><div class="stat-foot"><em>↗ Keep it going</em> · across your courses</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-top">Study time today<span class="stat-icon">◷</span></div><div class="stat-num">${Math.floor(mins/60)}h ${mins%60}m</div><div class="stat-foot">Active study, saved on this device</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-top">Quiz attempts<span class="stat-icon">✓</span></div><div class="stat-num">${Object.values(db.attempts||{}).reduce((a,x)=>a+(x.count||1),0)}</div><div class="stat-foot">${quizzes?`${quizzes} course${quizzes===1?'':'s'} practised so far`:'Ready when you are'}</div></div></div>`}
function courseCard(c,compact=false){const p=pct(c);return `<article class="course-card" data-course="${esc(c.id)}"><div class="course-top"><span class="course-icon">${icon(c)}</span><span class="badge">${esc(c.level||'Beginner')}</span></div><h3>${esc(c.title)}</h3><div class="course-meta">${esc(c.category)} · ${c.lessons} lessons · ${c.minutes} min</div><div class="progress-row"><span>${(db.enrolled||[]).includes(c.id)?'Your progress':'Course progress'}</span><b>${p}%</b></div><div class="progress-bar"><div class="progress-fill" style="width:${p}%"></div></div><div class="course-bottom"><span>♙ ${(c.students||0).toLocaleString()} learners</span><span>${p===100?'✓ Completed':'Continue learning →'}</span></div>${!compact&&db.role==='admin'?`<div class="admin-edit"><input placeholder="Edit title" aria-label="New course title" class="edit-title"><button class="secondary-btn" data-edit="${esc(c.id)}">Save</button></div>`:''}</article>`}
function renderView(){switch(view){case'Overview':return overview();case'My learning':return viewCourse?courseDetail():catalog(true);case'Explore courses':return catalog(false);case'Courses':return adminCoursesPage();case'Practice quiz':return quizPage();case'Flashcards':return flashcardsPage();case'Study planner':return plannerPage();case'My notes':return notesPage();case'Achievements':return achievementsPage();case'Career roadmap':return roadmapPage();case'Assignments':return assignmentsPage();case'Live classes':return livePage();case'Ebooks':return booksPage();case'AI tutor':return tutorPage();case'Analytics':return analyticsPage();case'Students':return studentsPage();case'Settings':return settingsPage();default:return overview()}}
function adminCoursesPage(){return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Course management</h1><p>Add, edit or remove courses for every student.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Add a course</h3><form id="admin-course-form"><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap"><label class="field" style="flex:1;min-width:180px">Course name<input id="admin-course-title" required maxlength="100" placeholder="e.g. Cloud Computing"></label><label class="field" style="width:190px">Subject area<select id="admin-course-category" class="search-input" style="width:100%"><option>Computer Science</option><option>Engineering</option><option>Mathematics</option><option>Physics</option><option>Electrical</option><option>Mechanical</option></select></label></div><label class="field">Short description<input id="admin-course-description" maxlength="500" placeholder="What will students learn?"></label><label class="field">Modules (comma-separated)<input id="admin-course-topics" required maxlength="1000" placeholder="Foundations, core concepts, projects, review"></label><button class="primary-btn" style="margin-top:12px">+ Add course for students</button></form></div><div class="section-head" style="margin-top:23px"><h2>All courses</h2><span class="course-meta">${allCourses().length} subjects</span></div><div class="wide-course-grid">${allCourses().map(c=>`<article class="course-card" data-course="${esc(c.id)}"><div class="course-visual">${icon(c)}</div><div class="course-top"><span class="badge">${esc(c.category)}</span><span class="course-meta">${esc(c.level||'Beginner')}</span></div><h3>${esc(c.title)}</h3><div class="course-meta">${esc(c.description||'')}</div><div class="admin-edit"><button class="secondary-btn" data-admin-course-edit="${esc(c.id)}">Edit course</button><button class="secondary-btn" data-admin-course-delete="${esc(c.id)}" style="color:#a34141">Delete</button></div></article>`).join('')}</div>`}
let focusRemaining=25*60,focusHandle=null,focusRunning=false;
function formatClock(seconds){return`${String(Math.floor(seconds/60)).padStart(2,'0')}:${String(seconds%60).padStart(2,'0')}`}
function plannerPage(){const today=new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10),tasks=(db.planner||[]).filter(t=>t.date===today),done=tasks.filter(t=>t.done).length;return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Study planner</h1><p>Turn big goals into smaller study sessions. Your plan is private to your account.</p></div><div class="content-grid"><div class="panel"><div class="section-head"><h2>Plan a study task</h2><span class="badge">${done}/${tasks.length} done today</span></div><form id="planner-form"><label class="field">What would you like to work on?<input id="task-title" required maxlength="120" placeholder="e.g. Practise binary trees"></label><div style="display:flex;gap:10px"><label class="field" style="flex:1">Course<select id="task-course" class="search-input" style="width:100%">${allCourses().map(c=>`<option value="${esc(c.id)}">${esc(c.title)}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><label class="field" style="width:130px">Date<input id="task-date" type="date" value="${today}" required></label></div><label class="field">Planned minutes<input id="task-minutes" type="number" min="10" max="240" value="25" required></label><button class="primary-btn" style="margin-top:14px">+ Add to my plan</button></form><div class="divider"></div><h3>Today’s plan</h3>${tasks.map((t,i)=>`<div class="planner-task ${t.done?'done':''}"><input class="task-check" type="checkbox" data-task-done="${esc(t.id)}" ${t.done?'checked':''} aria-label="Mark ${esc(t.title)} complete"><span class="planner-name">${esc(t.title)}</span><span class="course-meta">${t.minutes} min</span><button class="icon-button" data-task-delete="${esc(t.id)}" aria-label="Delete task">×</button></div>`).join('')||'<div class="empty">No tasks planned today yet. Add one small study goal to begin.</div>'}</div><aside class="panel"><h3>Focus timer</h3><p class="course-meta">Work in focused intervals, then take a short screen break.</p><div class="focus-clock" id="focus-clock">${formatClock(focusRemaining)}</div><label class="field">Focus interval<select id="focus-duration" class="search-input" style="width:100%"><option value="25">25 minutes · Pomodoro</option><option value="50">50 minutes · Deep focus</option></select></label><div style="display:flex;gap:8px;margin-top:13px"><button class="primary-btn" id="focus-toggle">${focusRunning?'Pause focus':'Start focus'}</button><button class="secondary-btn" id="focus-reset">Reset</button></div><div class="notice" style="margin-top:17px">Only completed focus sessions count toward your active study history. Leaving the page does not stop the timer.</div><h3 style="margin-top:20px">Your study streak</h3><div class="stat-num">🔥 ${studyStreak()} day${studyStreak()===1?'':'s'}</div><p class="course-meta">Practice a little regularly to build a routine.</p></aside></div>`}
function studyStreak(){const dates=new Set((db.activity||[]).map(a=>new Date(a.at).toLocaleDateString('en-CA')));let streak=0,d=new Date();for(let i=0;i<400;i++){const key=d.toLocaleDateString('en-CA');if(!dates.has(key)){if(i===0){d.setDate(d.getDate()-1);continue}break}streak++;d.setDate(d.getDate()-1)}return streak}
function notesPage(){return `<div class="page-title"><h1>My notes</h1><p>Keep useful explanations and revision notes with your courses.</p></div><div class="content-grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Write a study note</h3><form id="notes-form"><label class="field">Course<select id="note-course" class="search-input" style="width:100%">${allCourses().map(c=>`<option value="${esc(c.id)}">${esc(c.title)}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><label class="field">Title<input id="note-title" maxlength="100" placeholder="e.g. Binary search checklist" required></label><label class="field">Your note<textarea id="note-body" class="search-input" rows="6" maxlength="12000" placeholder="Add an example, formula, question, or explanation…" required style="resize:vertical"></textarea></label><button class="primary-btn" style="margin-top:12px">Save note</button></form><div class="notice">Notes belong to your account. Avoid storing passwords or private personal information in study notes.</div></div><div class="panel"><div class="section-head"><h3>Saved notes</h3><span class="badge">${(db.notes||[]).length}</span></div>${(db.notes||[]).slice().reverse().map(n=>`<article class="note-card"><div class="course-bottom"><b>${esc(n.title)}</b><button class="icon-button" data-note-delete="${esc(n.id)}" aria-label="Delete note">×</button></div><div class="course-meta">${esc(allCourses().find(c=>c.id===n.course)?.title||'Course note')} · ${new Date(n.at).toLocaleDateString()}</div><p>${esc(n.body)}</p></article>`).join('')||'<div class="empty">Your course notes will appear here after you save one.</div>'}</div></div>`}
function roadmapPage(){const paths=[{title:'Programming & problem solving',ids:['dsa','ml','ai'],description:'Write efficient code, reason about data, and build a portfolio of small projects.'},{title:'Mathematical foundations',ids:['math','calc'],description:'Strengthen calculus, linear algebra and probability for engineering and machine learning.'},{title:'Engineering systems',ids:['physics','electronics','materials'],description:'Connect foundational science to systems, devices and practical design.'}];return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Skills roadmap</h1><p>A practical map from core concepts to projects and career-ready habits.</p></div><div class="notice">Suggested order, not a grade or prediction. Choose paths that match your degree and interests.</div><div class="content-grid"><div>${paths.map((p,i)=>{const related=p.ids.map(id=>allCourses().find(c=>c.id===id)).filter(Boolean),score=related.length?Math.round(related.reduce((s,c)=>s+pct(c),0)/related.length):0;return `<article class="panel"><div class="section-head"><h2>${esc(p.title)}</h2><span class="badge">${score}% course progress</span></div><p class="course-meta">${esc(p.description)}</p><div class="progress-bar" style="margin:13px 0 17px"><div class="progress-fill" style="width:${score}%"></div></div>${related.map((c,j)=>`<div class="skill-step"><span class="skill-num">${pct(c)===100?'✓':j+1}</span><div style="flex:1"><b style="font-size:12px">${esc(c.title)}</b><div class="course-meta" style="margin-top:4px">${esc(c.topics?.slice(0,2).join(' · ')||c.category)}</div></div><button class="text-btn" data-roadmap-course="${esc(c.id)}">${isEnrolled(c.id)?'Continue →':'Explore →'}</button></div>`).join('')}</article>`}).join('')}</div><aside class="panel"><h3>Career-ready habits</h3>${[['Build proof','Save small projects in a portfolio or version-controlled repository.'],['Explain your choices','Practise describing assumptions, trade-offs and results.'],['Keep fundamentals fresh','Use short quizzes to revisit concepts over time.'],['Work with others','Review peers’ work and learn clear technical communication.']].map((x,i)=>`<div class="skill-step"><span class="skill-num">${i+1}</span><div><b style="font-size:12px">${x[0]}</b><div class="course-meta" style="margin-top:4px">${x[1]}</div></div></div>`).join('')}<div class="notice">Roadmap suggestions are general learning guidance, not a guarantee of employment or placement.</div></aside></div>`}
function overview(){const enrolled=allCourses().filter(c=>(db.enrolled||[]).includes(c.id));const recent=[...enrolled].sort((a,b)=>pct(b)-pct(a)).slice(0,4);const lessons=[['◉','AC circuits: impedance & phasors','Circuit Theory · 18 min'],['▣','Entropy and the second law','Thermodynamics · 24 min'],['⌘','Stacks and queue patterns','Data Structures · 16 min']];const sessions=db.meetings||[];return `<div class="welcome-row"><div><h1>Good ${new Date().getHours()<12?'morning':new Date().getHours()<17?'afternoon':'evening'}, ${esc(db.name.split(' ')[0])} <span>✦</span></h1><p>Small steps add up. Here’s your learning space for today.</p></div><div class="date-tag">◷ &nbsp;${new Date().toLocaleDateString('en',{weekday:'short',month:'short',day:'numeric'})}</div></div>${stats()}<div class="hero-banner"><div><div class="eyebrow">YOUR LEARNING JOURNEY</div><h2>${db.role==='admin'?'Make learning easy to navigate.':'A little progress goes a long way.'}</h2><p>${db.role==='admin'?'Review your courses, assignments and learner activity.':'Pick up where you left off or discover your next course.'}</p></div><button class="primary-btn" data-go="${db.role==='admin'?'Courses':'My learning'}">${db.role==='admin'?'Manage courses':'Continue learning'} &nbsp; →</button></div><div class="content-grid"><div><div class="section-head"><h2>${db.role==='admin'?'Course overview':'Continue learning'}</h2><button class="text-btn" data-go="${db.role==='admin'?'Courses':'My learning'}">See all courses →</button></div><div class="course-grid">${(recent.length?recent:allCourses().slice(0,2)).map(c=>courseCard(c)).join('')}</div>${db.role==='admin'?'<div class="admin-edit"><input id="new-course" placeholder="New course title"><button class="primary-btn" id="add-course">+ Add course</button></div>':''}</div><div class="side-panels"><div class="panel"><h3>Recent activity</h3>${(db.activity||[]).slice(-4).reverse().map(a=>`<div class="lesson-row"><div class="lesson-dot">${a.type==='quiz'?'✓':'◷'}</div><div class="lesson-copy"><b>${esc(a.label)}</b><span>${new Date(a.at).toLocaleString()}</span></div></div>`).join('')||lessons.map(l=>`<div class="lesson-row"><div class="lesson-dot">${l[0]}</div><div class="lesson-copy"><b>${l[1]}</b><span>${l[2]}</span></div></div>`).join('')}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Quick access</h3><div class="quick-actions"><button class="quick-action" data-go="Practice quiz"><b>✓ Take a quiz</b>Test your knowledge</button><button class="quick-action" data-go="AI tutor"><b>✳ Ask the tutor</b>Explore a concept</button><button class="quick-action" data-go="Ebooks"><b>▧ My reading</b>Open your library</button><button class="quick-action" data-go="Live classes"><b>◉ Class schedule</b>See upcoming sessions</button></div>${sessions.length?`<div class="notice">${sessions.length} live session${sessions.length===1?'':'s'} in your schedule</div>`:''}</div></div></div>`}
function catalog(onlyEnrolled){let list=allCourses().filter(c=>!onlyEnrolled||(db.enrolled||[]).includes(c.id));const cats=['All courses',...new Set(allCourses().map(c=>c.category))];if(!['All courses',...allCourses().map(c=>c.category)].includes(filter))filter='All courses';if(filter!=='All courses')list=list.filter(c=>c.category===filter);return `<div class="page-title"><h1>${onlyEnrolled?'My learning':'Explore courses'}</h1><p>${onlyEnrolled?'Your enrolled courses and current progress.':'Find your next engineering course and build real confidence.'}</p></div><div class="toolbar">${cats.map(c=>`<button class="filter-chip ${filter===c?'active':''}" data-filter="${esc(c)}">${esc(c)}</button>`).join('')}<span style="margin-left:auto;color:#87948c;font-size:11px">${list.length} courses</span></div><div class="wide-course-grid">${list.map(c=>`<article class="course-card" data-course="${esc(c.id)}"><div class="course-visual">${icon(c)}</div><div class="course-top"><span class="badge">${esc(c.category)}</span><span class="course-meta">${esc(c.level||'Beginner')}</span></div><h3>${esc(c.title)}</h3><div class="course-meta">${esc(c.description)}</div><div class="progress-row"><span>${(db.enrolled||[]).includes(c.id)?'Your progress':'Course outline'}</span><b>${(db.enrolled||[]).includes(c.id)?pct(c)+'%':c.topics?.length+' modules'}</b></div>${(db.enrolled||[]).includes(c.id)?`<div class="progress-bar"><div class="progress-fill" style="width:${pct(c)}%"></div></div>`:`<div class="course-meta">${c.lessons} lessons · ${c.minutes} min · ♙ ${(c.students||0).toLocaleString()}</div>`}<button class="primary-btn" data-enroll="${esc(c.id)}">${(db.enrolled||[]).includes(c.id)?'Open course →':'View course & enrol →'}</button></article>`).join('')||'<div class="empty">No courses here yet.</div>'}</div>`}
function courseModal(c){const enrolled=(db.enrolled||[]).includes(c.id);document.body.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<div class="modal-backdrop" id="modal-backdrop"><article class="modal"><button id="modal-close" class="icon-button modal-close">✕</button><div style="font-size:34px;margin-bottom:8px">${icon(c)}</div><span class="badge">${esc(c.category)} · ${esc(c.level||'Beginner')}</span><h2 style="margin-top:12px">${esc(c.title)}</h2><p>${esc(c.description)}</p><b style="font-size:12px">What you’ll cover</b><ul style="font-size:12px;line-height:2;color:#63776b">${(c.topics||[]).map(x=>`<li>${esc(x)}</li>`).join('')}</ul><div class="divider"></div><p>${c.lessons} lessons &nbsp; · &nbsp; ${c.minutes} minutes &nbsp; · &nbsp; ${(c.students||0).toLocaleString()} learners</p><button class="primary-btn" style="width:100%" id="modal-enroll">${enrolled?'Start learning':'Enrol in this course'}</button></article></div>`);document.getElementById('modal-close').onclick=closeModal;document.getElementById('modal-backdrop').onclick=e=>{if(e.target.id==='modal-backdrop')closeModal()};document.getElementById('modal-enroll').onclick=()=>{if(!enrolled){db.enrolled=[...new Set([...(db.enrolled||[]),c.id])];save();toast('You’re enrolled in '+c.title)}closeModal();openCourse(c.id)}}
function closeModal(){document.getElementById('modal-backdrop')?.remove()}
function openCourse(id){const c=allCourses().find(x=>x.id===id);if(!c)return;viewCourse=id;go('My learning')}
let viewCourse=null;
const LESSON_READINGS={
 dsa:[`Big O describes how an algorithm’s work grows as the input size n grows. O(1) stays constant, O(log n) grows slowly, O(n) examines each item, and O(n²) often compares every pair. Ignore constants when comparing growth rates.\n\nWorked example: scanning an unsorted list once is O(n); a nested loop over every pair is O(n²).`,`Arrays store items in order and give O(1) access by index; inserting near the beginning can take O(n). A stack is last-in, first-out (LIFO); a queue is first-in, first-out (FIFO).\n\nWorked example: a browser’s Back action can use a stack; a print queue uses FIFO.`,`A tree represents parent-child relationships. A binary search tree keeps smaller keys on the left and larger keys on the right. A graph represents vertices connected by edges; breadth-first search explores by layers, while depth-first search explores a path before backtracking.\n\nPractice: sketch a graph of your campus rooms and corridors.`,`Sorting organizes data; searching finds a value. Binary search repeatedly halves a sorted range and takes O(log n); it is incorrect on unsorted data. Merge sort runs in O(n log n) and uses extra memory; quicksort is often fast but has a quadratic worst case.`,`Recursion solves smaller instances of a problem and needs a base case to stop. Dynamic programming stores answers to overlapping subproblems instead of recalculating them.\n\nWorked example: Fibonacci recursion repeats many calculations; memoization stores each result once, reducing the work to O(n).`],
 ml:[`A machine-learning example is represented by features (inputs) and often a label (the target to predict). Clean missing values, check units, inspect distributions, and split training and test data before evaluating a model. Do not let test data influence training.`,`Linear regression predicts a numeric value with a weighted sum of features. Logistic regression converts a weighted sum to a probability for classification. The training algorithm adjusts weights to reduce a loss function.\n\nExample: use study hours as a feature to estimate a numeric exam score; choose a classification model to predict pass/fail.`,`Decision trees split examples using feature-based questions. Ensembles combine models: random forests average many trees, and boosting builds trees that correct previous errors. More complex models may improve fit but need careful validation.`,`A training set fits the model; a validation set helps choose model settings; a test set estimates final performance. Accuracy can mislead on imbalanced data, so also inspect precision, recall and the confusion matrix.`,`Overfitting occurs when a model learns noise in training examples and performs poorly on new data. Use simpler models, more representative data, regularization, or cross-validation. Always compare training and held-out results.`],
 ai:[`An intelligent agent observes an environment, chooses an action, then observes what changed. A useful problem definition includes the start state, legal actions, goal test and cost. Clear problem definitions help make search methods measurable.`,`Breadth-first search explores shallow states first; depth-first search uses less memory but may follow a long path. A heuristic estimates distance to the goal. A* combines cost so far with estimated remaining cost to guide useful paths.`,`Knowledge can be represented as facts and rules. A system can use inference rules to derive new facts. Search is useful when many choices exist; explicit knowledge helps explain conclusions and capture domain constraints.`,`Machine learning finds patterns from data instead of relying only on hand-written rules. Supervised learning uses labelled examples; unsupervised learning looks for structure without labels; reinforcement learning learns from action outcomes and rewards.`,`Trustworthy AI work checks data quality, privacy, bias, security and human impact throughout design and deployment. Test systems across relevant groups and settings, explain limitations, and provide a way to report failures.`],
 math:[`A Laplace transform changes a time-domain function into an s-domain expression. It is especially useful for linear differential equations with initial conditions because differentiation becomes algebra plus initial-value terms.`,`A Fourier series represents a periodic signal as a sum of sine and cosine waves. Each coefficient measures the amount of a frequency. This reveals frequency content in vibration, circuits and communication signals.`,`A differential equation relates a function to its derivatives. The order is the highest derivative present. Initial conditions select the particular solution that matches the physical starting state.`,`A complex number has real and imaginary parts. Euler’s formula links exponentials and sinusoids, which makes complex numbers practical for analysing AC magnitude and phase.`, `Check every transformation by checking its assumptions, initial values and units. After solving an engineering equation, substitute the result back into the original relation when possible.`],
 calc:[`A limit describes the value a function approaches near a point. Limits define continuity and derivatives. For f(x)=x², the change from x to x+h divided by h approaches 2x as h approaches zero.`,`The derivative measures instantaneous rate of change and the slope of a tangent. Use the product, quotient and chain rules carefully; the chain rule is essential when one function is inside another.`,`An integral accumulates quantity and can calculate area. The definite integral adds contributions over an interval; the Fundamental Theorem connects integration to antiderivatives and derivatives.`,`Partial derivatives measure change with respect to one input while holding others fixed. The gradient points in the direction of steepest increase and is used in optimization.`,`Use calculus to connect a model to a design decision: identify the quantity to optimize, write its constraints, differentiate, solve for candidates, and check boundary cases.`],
 physics:[`Use SI units and keep them through calculations. A vector has magnitude and direction; resolve it into components before adding forces or velocities. Dimensional analysis catches many mistakes early.`,`Newton’s laws relate forces and motion. A free-body diagram shows each external force. Work is force along displacement; changing work changes kinetic energy.`,`A wave transports energy. Wave speed equals frequency times wavelength. Resonance occurs when a system is driven near a natural frequency and can produce large responses.`,`Electric fields describe force per unit charge. Voltage is energy per charge; current is charge flow per time. In a simple resistor, V=IR. Check polarity and units when solving circuits.`,`Models have limits. Compare assumptions (ideal, frictionless, uniform material) with the physical system, then estimate how much they may affect an engineering result.`],
 electronics:[`Boolean algebra represents digital logic using 0 and 1. Learn truth tables for AND, OR and NOT, then apply De Morgan’s laws to simplify equivalent expressions.`,`A logic gate implements a Boolean operation. NAND and NOR are universal gates: any Boolean function can be built from either type. Check a circuit by writing its truth table.`,`Combinational circuit outputs depend only on current inputs. Simplify expressions, draw gates, and test all input combinations; decoders, adders and multiplexers are common building blocks.`,`A flip-flop stores one bit of state. Sequential circuits use a clock so counters and registers update predictably. Consider setup time, reset behaviour and the clock edge.`],
 materials:[`Crystal structure describes how atoms repeat in a solid. Unit cells are a compact description of that arrangement. Packing and structure influence density and some physical properties.`,`Stress is force per area; strain is relative deformation. The elastic region is reversible; plastic deformation remains after unloading. A stress–strain curve measures stiffness, strength and ductility.`,`Phase diagrams map stable phases against conditions such as temperature and composition. Read axes and boundaries carefully; cooling rate can affect the resulting microstructure.`,`Choose materials by matching requirements such as strength, weight, temperature, corrosion, manufacturability and cost. A good selection records trade-offs and safety factors.`]
};
function lessonReading(c,i){const lesson=LESSON_READINGS[c.id]?.[i];if(lesson)return lesson;const topic=c.topics?.[i]||c.title;return `${topic} is a core idea in ${c.title}. Start by defining the problem, listing known quantities and assumptions, then select the relevant rule or model. Keep track of units and check that each step follows from the previous one.\n\nStudy example: write a small worked example from your lecture notes, explain why each formula applies, and then solve a similar example with different values.\n\nPractice: summarize this topic in your own words and note one question to ask in class.`}
function showLesson(id,index){const c=allCourses().find(x=>x.id===id);if(!c)return;const topic=c.topics?.[index]||c.title,reading=lessonReading(c,index),closeLesson=()=>document.getElementById('lesson-modal-backdrop')?.remove();document.body.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<div class="modal-backdrop" id="lesson-modal-backdrop"><article class="modal lesson-modal"><button id="lesson-close" class="icon-button modal-close" aria-label="Close lesson">✕</button><span class="badge">${esc(c.title)} · MODULE ${index+1}</span><h2 style="margin-top:12px">${esc(topic)}</h2><div class="lesson-reading">${reading.split(/\n\n+/).map(p=>`<p>${esc(p)}</p>`).join('')}</div><div class="notice">Take a moment to connect the idea to a worked problem from your class materials.</div><button class="primary-btn" id="lesson-complete" data-cid="${esc(c.id)}" data-index="${index}">${moduleDone(c,index)?'✓ Completed — review':'Mark lesson complete'}</button></article></div>`);document.getElementById('lesson-close').onclick=closeLesson;document.getElementById('lesson-modal-backdrop').onclick=e=>{if(e.target.id==='lesson-modal-backdrop')closeLesson()};const complete=document.getElementById('lesson-complete');if(moduleDone(c,index)){complete.disabled=true}else complete.onclick=()=>{closeLesson();completeLesson(c.id,index)}}
function moduleDone(c,i){return (db.completed||[]).includes(`${c.id}:${i}`)}
function courseDetail(){const c=allCourses().find(x=>x.id===viewCourse);if(!c){viewCourse=null;return catalog(true)}const p=pct(c);return `<button class="text-btn" data-back-courses>← Back to courses</button><div class="page-title" style="margin-top:17px"><span style="font-size:36px">${icon(c)}</span><h1>${esc(c.title)}</h1><p>${esc(c.description)}</p></div><div class="content-grid"><div class="panel"><div class="section-head"><h2>Course modules</h2><span class="badge">${p}% complete</span></div><div class="progress-bar"><div class="progress-fill" style="width:${p}%"></div></div>${(c.topics||[]).map((topic,i)=>`<div class="assignment-row"><div class="lesson-dot">${moduleDone(c,i)?'✓':'▶'}</div><div><b>${i+1}. ${esc(topic)}</b><p>Module ${i+1} · ${Math.max(8,Math.round(c.minutes/c.topics.length))} min · Reading, example & practice</p></div><button class="secondary-btn" data-lesson="${i}" data-cid="${esc(c.id)}">${moduleDone(c,i)?'Review':'Start lesson'}</button></div>`).join('')}<button class="primary-btn" data-course-quiz="${esc(c.id)}">✓ &nbsp; Take course quiz</button></div><div class="panel"><h3>Course resources</h3><div class="lesson-row"><div class="lesson-dot">▧</div><div class="lesson-copy"><b>Course reading & notes</b><span>Open the ebook reader</span></div><button class="text-btn" data-go="Ebooks">Open →</button></div><div class="divider"></div><h3>Learning goal</h3><p class="course-meta">Read the short lesson, work through the example, then try the practice question. Your progress changes when you mark a lesson complete.</p></div></div>`}
function quizPage(){if(quizState)return renderQuiz();const last=Object.entries(db.attempts||{}).sort((a,b)=>new Date(b[1].at)-new Date(a[1].at));return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Practice quiz</h1><p>Five questions. A small, focused way to check your understanding.</p></div><div class="quiz-wrap"><div class="panel"><h3>Choose a course</h3>${allCourses().map(c=>`<div class="assignment-row"><div class="lesson-dot">${icon(c)}</div><div><b>${esc(c.title)}</b><p>5 questions · ${esc(c.category)}${db.attempts[c.id]?` · Best score: ${db.attempts[c.id].best}/5`:''}</p></div><button class="primary-btn" data-start-quiz="${esc(c.id)}">Start quiz →</button></div>`).join('')}</div>${last.length?`<div class="panel"><h3>Recent results</h3>${last.slice(0,3).map(([id,a])=>`<div class="lesson-row"><div class="lesson-dot">✓</div><div class="lesson-copy"><b>${esc(allCourses().find(c=>c.id===id)?.title||id)}</b><span>Score: ${a.score}/5 · ${new Date(a.at).toLocaleString()}</span></div><span class="badge">Best ${a.best}/5</span></div>`).join('')}</div>`:''}</div>`}
function beginQuiz(id){const c=allCourses().find(x=>x.id===id);if(!c)return;go('Practice quiz');quizState={id,index:0,answers:Array(c.quiz.length).fill(null),started:Date.now()};document.querySelector('.page').innerHTML=renderQuiz();bindView()}
function renderQuiz(){const c=allCourses().find(x=>x.id===quizState.id);if(!c)return quizPage();if(quizState.index>=c.quiz.length){const score=quizState.answers.reduce((s,x,i)=>s+(x===c.quiz[i][2]?1:0),0),old=db.attempts[c.id]||{best:0,count:0};db.attempts[c.id]={score,best:Math.max(score,old.best||0),count:(old.count||0)+1,at:new Date().toISOString()};db.activity=[...(db.activity||[]),{type:'quiz',label:`${c.title} quiz · ${score}/5`,at:new Date().toISOString(),minutes:Math.max(1,Math.round((Date.now()-quizState.started)/60000))}];if(score===5)db.progress[c.id]=Math.min(100,pct(c)+10);save();quizState.done={score};return renderQuiz()}if(quizState.done){let score=quizState.done.score;return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Quiz complete</h1><p>${esc(c.title)} · Your practice result</p></div><div class="quiz-wrap panel result"><div style="font-size:35px">${score>=4?'🎉':'🌱'}</div><div class="score">${score}<span style="font-size:21px;color:#8a9990"> / 5</span></div><h2>${score>=4?'Well done!':'Good practice'}</h2><p class="course-meta">${score===5?'A perfect score. You have a great grasp of these ideas.':score>=3?'You’re building a solid foundation. Review any tricky topics and try again.':'Practice helps ideas stick. Review the course topics and have another go.'}</p><button class="primary-btn" id="quiz-retry">Try again</button> <button class="secondary-btn" id="quiz-exit">Back to quizzes</button></div>`}const q=c.quiz[quizState.index];return `<div class="page-title"><button class="text-btn" id="quiz-exit">← Exit quiz</button><h1>${esc(c.title)}</h1><p>Knowledge check · Question ${quizState.index+1} of ${c.quiz.length}</p></div><div class="quiz-wrap quiz-card"><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:11px;color:#849189"><span>QUESTION ${quizState.index+1}</span><span>${c.quiz.length-quizState.index} TO GO</span></div><div class="quiz-progress"><div style="width:${quizState.index/c.quiz.length*100}%"></div></div><div class="quiz-question">${esc(q[0])}</div>${q[1].map((o,i)=>`<label class="option ${quizState.answers[quizState.index]===i?'selected':''}"><input type="radio" name="answer" value="${i}" ${quizState.answers[quizState.index]===i?'checked':''}>${esc(o)}</label>`).join('')}<div class="quiz-footer"><span class="course-meta">No time limit · Take your time</span><button class="primary-btn" id="quiz-next">${quizState.index===c.quiz.length-1?'Finish quiz':'Next question →'}</button></div></div>`}
function assignmentsPage(){return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Assignments</h1><p>Course practice tasks and upcoming work in one place.</p></div><div class="content-grid"><div class="panel"><div class="section-head"><h2>${db.role==='admin'?'Manage assignments':'Your assignments'}</h2>${db.role==='admin'?'<button class="text-btn" id="new-assignment">+ Create</button>':''}</div>${(db.assignments||[]).map((a,i)=>`<div class="assignment-row"><div class="lesson-dot">${a.status==='Submitted'?'✓':'▣'}</div><div><b>${esc(a.title)}</b><p>${esc(a.course)} · Due ${esc(a.due||'No deadline')} · ${esc(a.points||10)} points</p></div>${db.role==='admin'?`<span class="badge">${a.submitted||0} submitted</span>`:`<label class="secondary-btn" style="cursor:pointer">${a.status==='Submitted'?'Submitted · re-upload':'Submit work'}<input class="assignment-upload" data-id="${i}" type="file" hidden></label>`}</div>`).join('')||'<div class="empty">No assignments have been posted yet.</div>'}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Helpful reminder</h3><div class="notice">Your assignment submissions are saved to this browser as a demo. A connected database and private file storage are needed to submit real work.</div><button class="quick-action" style="width:100%" data-go="Explore courses"><b>Explore your courses</b>Keep learning and find an assignment</button></div></div>`}
function livePage(){const now=new Date();return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Online classes & webinars</h1><p>Join a live session or add a class of your own.</p></div><div class="content-grid"><div class="panel"><div class="section-head"><h2>Upcoming sessions</h2><button class="text-btn" id="add-session">+ Add session</button></div>${(db.meetings||[]).map((m,i)=>`<div class="assignment-row upcoming"><div class="lesson-dot">◉</div><div><b>${esc(m.title)}</b><p>${esc(m.date)} · ${esc(m.time||'Class session')} · ${esc(m.host||'Course instructor')}</p></div><a class="primary-btn" href="${/^https:\/\//i.test(m.url||'')?esc(m.url):'#'}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" ${/^https:\/\//i.test(m.url||'')?'':'aria-disabled="true"'}>${m.attending?'✓ Registered':'Join class →'}</a></div>`).join('')||'<div class="empty">Your upcoming classes will appear here. Add a video conference link to schedule a session.</div>'}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Classroom notes</h3><div class="notice">For a real webinar, add a trusted video call URL from your institution’s meeting provider. Vinedu does not host video calls.</div><h3>Study activity</h3><p class="course-meta">Vinedu measures study from active learning interactions and quiz attempts. Simply keeping a tab open does not count as attendance or learning.</p></div></div>`}
function booksPage(){return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Ebook library</h1><p>A calm reading space for course notes and engineering references.</p></div><div class="content-grid"><div class="panel"><div class="section-head"><h2>Reading shelf</h2><label class="primary-btn" style="cursor:pointer">Open a text file<input type="file" id="book-upload" accept=".txt,.md,.csv,text/plain" hidden></label></div>${allCourses().slice(0,4).map(c=>`<div class="assignment-row"><div class="lesson-dot">▧</div><div><b>${esc(c.title)} · Reading notes</b><p>${esc(c.category)} · Course resource &nbsp; ${db.bookmarks.includes(c.id)?'· 🔖 Saved':''}</p></div><button class="secondary-btn" data-read="${esc(c.id)}">Read →</button><button class="icon-button" data-bookmark="${esc(c.id)}">${db.bookmarks.includes(c.id)?'🔖':'☆'}</button></div>`).join('')}<div class="divider"></div><h3>Your reading room</h3><article class="reader-box" id="reader">${esc(readerText).replace(/\n/g,'<br>')}</article></div><aside class="panel"><h3>Reading intelligence</h3><div class="notice">Text, Markdown and CSV files open locally in your browser; they are not uploaded to a server. This starter does not extract text from scanned PDFs or run OCR.</div><h3>Built for steady study</h3><p class="course-meta">Save a reading for later with the bookmark icon. Course notes are illustrative placeholders: add your institution-approved ebook materials before sharing the app with students.</p><div class="lesson-row"><div class="lesson-dot">🔖</div><div class="lesson-copy"><b>${db.bookmarks.length} saved reading${db.bookmarks.length===1?'':'s'}</b><span>Ready for later</span></div></div></aside></div>`}
function tutorPage(){return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Your study tutor <span class="badge">Course-aware demo</span></h1><p>Ask about a concept. Answers draw on the sample course outlines included here.</p></div><div class="content-grid"><div class="panel chatbox"><div class="section-head"><h3>Vinedu study chat</h3><button class="text-btn" id="clear-chat">Clear chat</button></div><div class="chat-messages" id="chat-messages">${chatLog.length?chatLog.map(m=>`<div class="bubble ${m.role}">${esc(m.text)}</div>`).join(''):'<div class="bubble">Hi! Pick a topic and I’ll help you study it. This demo tutor uses the sample course outlines stored in your browser, and shows relevant course references when possible. Try “Explain Kirchhoff’s laws” or “Help me with entropy”.</div>'}</div><form id="chat-form" class="chat-input-row"><input id="chat-input" required placeholder="Ask a course question…" autocomplete="off"><button class="primary-btn">Ask →</button></form></div><aside class="panel"><h3>Study suggestions</h3>${['Explain a topic simply','Quiz me on my latest course','What should I learn about circuits?'].map(s=>`<button class="quick-action suggestion" style="width:100%;margin-bottom:8px" data-prompt="${esc(s)}">${esc(s)} →</button>`).join('')}<div class="notice">For AI-generated RAG answers, configure a private backend with institutional documents, permission-aware search and a secured model API key. Never put a secret key in browser code.</div><label class="field">Use course context<select id="tutor-course" class="search-input" style="width:100%"><option value="all">All course outlines</option>${allCourses().map(c=>`<option value="${esc(c.id)}">${esc(c.title)}</option>`).join('')}</select></label></aside></div>`}
function analyticsPage(){const ac=db.activity||[];const days=Array.from({length:7},(_,i)=>{const d=new Date();d.setDate(d.getDate()-6+i);return {date:d,label:d.toLocaleDateString('en',{weekday:'short'}),items:ac.filter(a=>new Date(a.at).toDateString()===d.toDateString())}});const max=Math.max(1,...days.map(d=>d.items.reduce((s,a)=>s+(a.minutes||1),0)));return `<div class="page-title"><h1>${db.role==='admin'?'Learning analytics':'Your learning activity'}</h1><p>Activity comes from recorded learning actions and quiz attempts.</p></div><div class="stat-grid">${stats().match(/<div class="stat-card">[\s\S]*?<\/div><\/div>/g)?.slice(1).join('')||''}</div><div class="content-grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Active study · last 7 days</h3><div style="height:170px;display:flex;align-items:end;justify-content:space-around;gap:12px;padding:15px 5px">${days.map(d=>{const m=d.items.reduce((s,a)=>s+(a.minutes||1),0);return `<div style="flex:1;height:100%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:end;flex-direction:column;gap:7px"><span style="font-size:9px;color:#849189">${m?m+'m':''}</span><div title="${m} minutes" style="height:${Math.max(5,m/max*92)}%;width:min(38px,70%);background:${m?'linear-gradient(#54b28a,#287a60)':'#edf1ed'};border-radius:7px 7px 3px 3px"></div><span class="course-meta">${d.label}</span></div>`}).join('')}</div></div><div class="panel"><h3>Course progress</h3>${allCourses().filter(c=>db.role==='admin'||db.enrolled.includes(c.id)).map(c=>`<div class="lesson-row"><div class="lesson-copy"><b>${esc(c.title)}</b><span>${db.attempts[c.id]?`Quiz best ${db.attempts[c.id].best}/5`:'Keep building your study streak'}</span><div class="progress-bar" style="margin-top:8px"><div class="progress-fill" style="width:${pct(c)}%"></div></div></div><span class="badge">${pct(c)}%</span></div>`).join('')}</div></div><div class="panel" style="margin-top:16px"><h3>Activity history <span class="course-meta">${ac.length} recorded interactions</span></h3>${ac.length?[...ac].reverse().slice(0,10).map(a=>`<div class="lesson-row"><div class="lesson-dot">${a.type==='quiz'?'✓':'◷'}</div><div class="lesson-copy"><b>${esc(a.label)}</b><span>${new Date(a.at).toLocaleString()} · ${a.minutes||1} min active study</span></div></div>`).join(''):'<p class="course-meta">Your course lessons and quiz attempts will be recorded here as you study. This view counts actions, not passive browser time.</p>'}</div>${db.role==='admin'?'<button class="secondary-btn" id="export-data">Export activity CSV</button>':''}`}
function studentsPage(){return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Students</h1><p>Accounts and learning activity from the shared Vinedu database.</p></div><div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-top">Courses in catalogue<span class="stat-icon">▤</span></div><div class="stat-num">${allCourses().length}</div><div class="stat-foot">Engineering, CS, math and physics</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-top">Students<span class="stat-icon">♙</span></div><div class="stat-num" id="student-total">—</div><div class="stat-foot">Registered student accounts</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-top">Your activity<span class="stat-icon">◷</span></div><div class="stat-num">${db.activity.length}</div><div class="stat-foot">Interactions on this account</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-top">Your quiz attempts<span class="stat-icon">✓</span></div><div class="stat-num">${Object.values(db.attempts).reduce((n,x)=>n+(x.count||1),0)}</div><div class="stat-foot">Saved to your account</div></div></div><div class="panel"><h3>Student accounts</h3><div id="student-list"><div class="course-meta">Loading registered students…</div></div></div>`}
async function loadStudents(){const target=document.getElementById('student-list');if(!target)return;try{const r=await fetch('/api/admin/students',{credentials:'same-origin',cache:'no-store'}),data=await r.json();if(!r.ok)throw Error(data.error);const total=document.getElementById('student-total');if(total)total.textContent=data.students.length;target.innerHTML=data.students.map(s=>`<div class="lesson-row"><div class="avatar">${esc(s.display_name[0]?.toUpperCase()||'S')}</div><div class="lesson-copy"><b>${esc(s.display_name)}</b><span>${esc(s.email)} · Joined ${new Date(s.created_at).toLocaleDateString()}</span></div><span class="badge">${s.enrolled} courses · ${s.quiz_courses} quizzes · ${s.is_blocked?'Blocked':'Active'}</span><button class="secondary-btn" data-student-block="${s.id}" data-blocked="${s.is_blocked}">${s.is_blocked?'Unblock':'Block'}</button></div>`).join('')||'<div class="empty">No student accounts yet. Share the student sign-up link to get started.</div>'}catch(e){target.innerHTML=`<div class="notice">${esc(e.message||'Could not load student accounts.')}</div>`}}
function settingsPage(){return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Settings</h1><p>Personalise your secure learning space.</p></div><div class="content-grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Your account</h3><label class="field">Display name<input id="setting-name" value="${esc(db.name)}"></label><label class="field">Email address<input id="setting-email" value="${esc(db.email)}" type="email" disabled></label><div class="notice">Signed in as ${db.role==='admin'?'administrator':'student'}. Ask your school administrator to change your account access.</div><button class="primary-btn" style="margin-top:17px" id="save-settings">Save display name</button><div class="divider"></div><h3>Study preferences</h3><label style="font-size:12px;color:#62756a"><input type="checkbox" id="pref-reminders" ${db.settings.reminders?'checked':''}> Show gentle study reminders</label></div><div class="panel"><h3>Your learning data</h3><p class="course-meta">Your progress, quiz scores and enrolments are saved to your Vinedu account.</p><button class="secondary-btn" id="download-data">Download a backup (JSON)</button><div class="divider"></div><button class="secondary-btn" id="reset-data" style="color:#a34141">Reset my learning progress</button><div class="notice">Your login session is stored in a secure, HTTP-only cookie. Sign out on shared devices.</div></div></div>`}
function bindView(){document.getElementById('logout')?.addEventListener('click',async()=>{await fetch('/api/logout',{method:'POST',credentials:'same-origin'});db={...defaults};view='Overview';viewCourse=null;renderLoginPage()});document.getElementById('home-mobile')?.addEventListener('click',()=>go('Overview'));document.getElementById('notif')?.addEventListener('click',()=>toast(db.activity.length?`You have ${db.activity.length} study activities recorded.`:'You’re all caught up!'));document.querySelectorAll('[data-go]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>go(b.dataset.go));document.querySelectorAll('[data-filter]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{filter=b.dataset.filter;document.querySelector('.page').innerHTML=renderView();bindView()});document.querySelectorAll('[data-course]').forEach(el=>el.onclick=e=>{if(e.target.closest('button,input'))return;const c=allCourses().find(x=>x.id===el.dataset.course);if(c)courseModal(c)});document.querySelectorAll('[data-enroll]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=e=>{e.stopPropagation();const c=allCourses().find(x=>x.id===b.dataset.enroll);if(c)courseModal(c)});document.querySelectorAll('[data-start-quiz]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>beginQuiz(b.dataset.startQuiz));document.querySelectorAll('[data-course-quiz]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>beginQuiz(b.dataset.courseQuiz));document.getElementById('quiz-next')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{if(quizState.answers[quizState.index]===null)return toast('Choose an answer to continue.');quizState.index++;document.querySelector('.page').innerHTML=renderQuiz();bindView()});document.querySelectorAll('input[name="answer"]').forEach(r=>r.onchange=()=>{quizState.answers[quizState.index]=Number(r.value);document.querySelector('.page').innerHTML=renderQuiz();bindView()});document.getElementById('quiz-exit')?.addEventListener('click',()=>go('Practice quiz'));document.getElementById('quiz-retry')?.addEventListener('click',()=>beginQuiz(quizState.id));document.getElementById('global-search')?.addEventListener('input',e=>{const q=e.target.value.trim().toLowerCase();if(q){if(view!=='Explore courses'&&view!=='Courses'&&view!=='My learning')view='Explore courses';const page=document.querySelector('.page');if(page){let list=allCourses().filter(c=>c.title.toLowerCase().includes(q)||c.category.toLowerCase().includes(q)||c.topics?.some(t=>t.toLowerCase().includes(q)));page.innerHTML=`<div class="page-title"><h1>Search results</h1><p>Courses matching “${esc(q)}”</p></div><div class="wide-course-grid">${list.map(c=>`<article class="course-card" data-course="${esc(c.id)}"><div class="course-visual">${icon(c)}</div><h3>${esc(c.title)}</h3><div class="course-meta">${esc(c.category)} · ${esc(c.description)}</div><button class="primary-btn" data-enroll="${esc(c.id)}">View course →</button></article>`).join('')||'<div class="empty">No courses match this search.</div>'}</div>`;bindView()}}});document.querySelectorAll('[data-back-courses]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{viewCourse=null;go('My learning')});document.querySelectorAll('[data-lesson]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>completeLesson(b.dataset.cid,Number(b.dataset.lesson)));document.querySelectorAll('[data-bookmark]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{const id=b.dataset.bookmark;db.bookmarks=db.bookmarks.includes(id)?db.bookmarks.filter(x=>x!==id):[...db.bookmarks,id];save();document.querySelector('.page').innerHTML=booksPage();bindView();toast(db.bookmarks.includes(id)?'Saved for later.':'Bookmark removed.')});document.querySelectorAll('[data-read]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>readCourse(b.dataset.read));document.getElementById('book-upload')?.addEventListener('change',async e=>{const f=e.target.files[0];if(!f)return;readerText=(await f.text()).slice(0,100000);document.getElementById('reader').innerHTML=esc(readerText).replace(/\n/g,'<br>');toast('Opened '+f.name+' locally.')});document.getElementById('chat-form')?.addEventListener('submit',e=>{e.preventDefault();const input=document.getElementById('chat-input');if(input.value.trim())sendTutor(input.value.trim())});document.querySelectorAll('[data-prompt]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>sendTutor(b.dataset.prompt));document.getElementById('clear-chat')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{chatLog=[];document.getElementById('chat-messages').innerHTML='<div class="bubble">Chat cleared. What topic shall we study?</div>'});document.getElementById('add-session')?.addEventListener('click',addSession);document.getElementById('new-assignment')?.addEventListener('click',addAssignment);document.querySelectorAll('.assignment-upload').forEach(el=>el.onchange=()=>{const f=el.files[0];if(!f)return;db.assignments[Number(el.dataset.id)].status='Submitted';db.assignments[Number(el.dataset.id)].file=f.name;save();document.querySelector('.page').innerHTML=assignmentsPage();bindView();toast('Demo submission saved: '+f.name)});document.getElementById('add-course')?.addEventListener('click',addCourse);document.querySelectorAll('[data-edit]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>editCourse(b.dataset.edit,b.parentElement.querySelector('input').value));document.getElementById('save-settings')?.addEventListener('click',saveSettings);document.getElementById('pref-reminders')?.addEventListener('change',e=>{db.settings.reminders=e.target.checked;save()});document.getElementById('download-data')?.addEventListener('click',()=>download('vinedu-backup.json',JSON.stringify(db,null,2),'application/json'));document.getElementById('export-data')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{const rows=[['time','type','activity','active minutes'],...(db.activity||[]).map(a=>[a.at,a.type,a.label,a.minutes])];download('vinedu-activity.csv',rows.map(r=>r.map(x=>'"'+String(x??'').replaceAll('"','""')+'"').join(',')).join('\n'),'text/csv')});document.getElementById('reset-data')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{if(confirm('Remove all your Vinedu learning data from your account?')){db={...defaults,name:db.name,email:db.email,role:db.role};save();go('Overview');toast('Your learning data was reset.')}});if(db.role==='admin'&&view==='Students')loadStudents()}
function completeLesson(id,i){const c=allCourses().find(x=>x.id===id);if(!c)return;const key=`${id}:${i}`;if(moduleDone(c,i))return;db.completed=[...(db.completed||[]),key];const count=c.topics?.length||1,done=db.completed.filter(x=>x.startsWith(`${id}:`)).length;db.progress[id]=Math.round(Math.min(100,done/count*100));db.activity=[...(db.activity||[]),{type:'lesson',label:`${c.title} · ${c.topics?.[i]||`Module ${i+1}`}`,at:new Date().toISOString(),minutes:Math.max(5,Math.round(c.minutes/count))}];save();toast('Lesson marked complete!');const target=document.querySelector('.page');target.innerHTML=courseDetail();bindView()}
function readCourse(id){const c=allCourses().find(x=>x.id===id);if(!c)return;readerText=`${c.title}\n\n${c.description}\n\nCourse outline\n${(c.topics||[]).map((x,i)=>`${i+1}. ${x}`).join('\n')}\n\nThese sample notes are an outline only. Add your institution-approved course reading materials for a real student library.`;const el=document.getElementById('reader');el.innerHTML=esc(readerText).replace(/\n/g,'<br>');el.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'})}
function sendTutor(input){chatLog.push({role:'user',text:input});const context=document.getElementById('tutor-course')?.value||'all';const q=input.toLowerCase();const relevant=allCourses().filter(c=>(context==='all'||c.id===context)&&(`${c.title} ${c.category} ${c.description} ${c.topics?.join(' ')}`).toLowerCase().split(/[^a-z0-9]+/).some(w=>w.length>3&&q.includes(w)));let answer;if(/quiz|test me|practice/.test(q))answer='Here’s a good next step: pick a course under Practice quiz and try its five-question knowledge check. Afterward, revisit the module that felt least familiar.';else if(/what.*learn|recommend|next/.test(q)){const c=allCourses().filter(x=>db.enrolled.includes(x.id)).sort((a,b)=>pct(a)-pct(b))[0];answer=c?`Your next suggested course is ${c.title}. You’ve completed ${pct(c)}% so far. Try its “${c.topics?.[0]}” module, then take the course quiz to check what stuck.`:'Explore courses and choose a topic that matches what you are studying this term.'}else if(relevant.length){const c=relevant[0];const topic=c.topics.find(t=>q.split(/[^a-z0-9]+/).some(w=>w.length>4&&t.toLowerCase().includes(w)));answer=`From the ${c.title} course outline${topic?` (topic: ${topic})`:''}: ${c.description} Course topics include ${c.topics.join('; ')}.\n\nTo work through it: first write down the known quantities, then identify the relevant law or definition, and check that your result has the correct units. This demo uses course summaries only, so check your approved notes for formal definitions and worked examples.`}else answer='I don’t see that topic in the course outlines currently loaded in this demo. Try a course keyword such as circuits, entropy, arrays, Laplace transforms, or materials. For grounded answers from institution-approved textbooks, connect a secured backend with permission-aware retrieval.';chatLog.push({role:'assistant',text:answer});const ac=db.activity||[];ac.push({type:'tutor',label:'Study tutor · '+input.slice(0,45),at:new Date().toISOString(),minutes:2});db.activity=ac;save();document.getElementById('chat-input').value='';const box=document.getElementById('chat-messages');box.innerHTML=chatLog.map(m=>`<div class="bubble ${m.role}">${esc(m.text)}</div>`).join('');box.scrollTop=box.scrollHeight}
function addSession(){const title=prompt('Session title');if(!title?.trim())return;const date=prompt('Date and time (for example: 5 Nov, 3:30 pm)','5 Nov, 3:30 pm');if(!date)return;const url=prompt('Secure meeting link (https://…)','https://');db.meetings=[...(db.meetings||[]),{title:title.trim(),date,time:'Live session',host:db.name,url:url?.startsWith('https://')?url:'',attending:false}];save();document.querySelector('.page').innerHTML=livePage();bindView();toast('Session added.')}
function addAssignment(){const title=prompt('Assignment title');if(!title?.trim())return;const course=prompt('Course name','Engineering practice')||'Engineering practice';const due=prompt('Due date (optional)','Friday')||'No deadline';db.assignments=[...(db.assignments||[]),{title:title.trim(),course,due,points:10,status:'Open',submitted:0}];save();document.querySelector('.page').innerHTML=assignmentsPage();bindView();toast('Assignment created.')}
function addCourse(){if(db.role==='admin'){go('Courses');return}const title=document.getElementById('new-course')?.value.trim();if(!title)return toast('Enter a course title first.');const id='course-'+Date.now();db.customCourses=[...(db.customCourses||[]),{id,title,category:'Engineering',icon:'📘',level:'Beginner',lessons:4,minutes:60,progress:0,students:0,description:`Explore ${title} with structured lessons and engineering practice.`,topics:['Introduction & foundations','Core concepts','Worked examples','Knowledge check'],quiz:courses[0].quiz}];save();document.querySelector('.page').innerHTML=overview();bindView();toast('Course added to the catalogue.')}
function editCourse(id,title){if(!title?.trim())return toast('Enter an updated course title.');const c=allCourses().find(x=>x.id===id);if(c)c.title=title.trim();save();const page=document.querySelector('.page');page.innerHTML=renderView();bindView();toast('Course updated.')}
function saveSettings(){const name=document.getElementById('setting-name').value.trim();const email=document.getElementById('setting-email').value.trim();if(!name||!email.includes('@'))return toast('Enter a name and valid email.');db.name=name;db.email=email;save();go('Settings');toast('Settings saved.')}
function download(name,data,type){const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([data],{type}));a.download=name;a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href),1000)}
async function init(){try{const cfg=await fetch('/api/config',{credentials:'same-origin',cache:'no-store'});if(cfg.ok)window.localDemoAdmin=(await cfg.json()).demoAdmin;await loadCatalog();const r=await fetch('/api/me',{credentials:'same-origin',cache:'no-store'});if(!r.ok)throw Error('Could not reach the Vinedu server. Check your connection and refresh.');const data=await r.json();if(data.user){db=prepareUser(data.user);saveQueue=Promise.resolve();go('Overview')}else renderLoginPage()}catch(e){window.authError=e.message||'Could not connect to Vinedu. Please refresh.';renderLoginPage()}}
installAdvancedHandlers();
installAdminHandlers();
installProfileMenu();
installAcademicHandlers();
installPhotoHandlers();
installStudyTools();
function decorateProfile(){document.querySelectorAll('.sidebar .avatar,.top-actions > .avatar').forEach(avatar=>{if(db.hasPhoto)avatar.innerHTML='<img class="avatar-image" src="/api/profile/photo" alt="">';else avatar.textContent=db.name[0]?.toUpperCase()||'V'});const avatar=document.querySelector('.top-actions > .avatar');if(!avatar)return;const wrap=document.createElement('div');wrap.className='profile-wrap';const toggle=document.createElement('button');toggle.type='button';toggle.id='profile-toggle';toggle.className='profile-trigger';toggle.setAttribute('aria-label','Open profile menu');toggle.setAttribute('aria-haspopup','menu');toggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false');const icon=avatar.cloneNode(true);icon.setAttribute('aria-hidden','true');toggle.append(icon);const menu=document.createElement('div');menu.id='profile-menu';menu.className='profile-menu';menu.hidden=true;menu.setAttribute('role','menu');const info=document.createElement('div');info.className='profile-menu-info';const name=document.createElement('b');name.textContent=db.name;const email=document.createElement('span');email.textContent=db.email;const role=document.createElement('small');role.textContent=db.role==='admin'?'Administrator':'Engineering student';info.append(name,email,role);const signout=document.createElement('button');signout.type='button';signout.id='profile-signout';signout.className='profile-logout';signout.setAttribute('role','menuitem');signout.textContent='↪  Sign out';menu.append(info,signout);wrap.append(toggle,menu);avatar.replaceWith(wrap)}
function decorateProfileSettings(){const panel=document.querySelector('.page .panel');if(!panel||document.getElementById('profile-photo-input'))return;panel.insertAdjacentHTML('afterbegin',`<div class="profile-photo-settings"><div class="avatar photo-preview">${db.hasPhoto?'<img class="avatar-image" src="/api/profile/photo" alt="Profile photo">':esc(db.name[0]?.toUpperCase()||'V')}</div><div><b>Profile photo</b><p class="course-meta">JPEG, PNG or WebP · up to 2 MB. Saved to your account.</p><label class="secondary-btn photo-pick">Choose photo<input id="profile-photo-input" type="file" accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp" hidden></label>${db.hasPhoto?'<button id="remove-profile-photo" class="text-btn" style="margin-left:10px">Remove photo</button>':''}</div></div><div class="divider"></div>`)}
function decorateCourseProgress(){document.querySelectorAll('.course-card[data-course]').forEach(card=>{const course=allCourses().find(c=>c.id===card.dataset.course);if(!course)return;const started=isCourseStarted(course.id),progress=pct(course);const label=card.querySelector('.progress-row span');if(label)label.textContent=started?'Your progress':'Not started';const value=card.querySelector('.progress-row b');if(value)value.textContent=`${progress}%`;const fill=card.querySelector('.progress-fill');if(fill)fill.style.width=`${progress}%`;const bottom=card.querySelector('.course-bottom span:last-child');if(bottom)bottom.textContent=progress===100?'✓ Completed':started?'Continue learning →':'Start learning →'})}
function courseModal(c){const started=isCourseStarted(c.id);document.body.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<div class="modal-backdrop" id="modal-backdrop"><article class="modal"><button id="modal-close" class="icon-button modal-close">✕</button><div style="font-size:34px;margin-bottom:8px">${icon(c)}</div><span class="badge">${esc(c.category)} · ${esc(c.level||'Beginner')}</span><h2 style="margin-top:12px">${esc(c.title)}</h2><p>${esc(c.description)}</p><b style="font-size:12px">What you’ll cover</b><ul style="font-size:12px;line-height:2;color:#63776b">${(c.topics||[]).map(x=>`<li>${esc(x)}</li>`).join('')}</ul><div class="divider"></div><p>${c.lessons} lessons &nbsp; · &nbsp; ${c.minutes} minutes &nbsp; · &nbsp; ${(c.students||0).toLocaleString()} learners</p><button class="primary-btn" style="width:100%" id="modal-enroll">${started?'Continue learning →':'Start learning'}</button></article></div>`);document.getElementById('modal-close').onclick=closeModal;document.getElementById('modal-backdrop').onclick=e=>{if(e.target.id==='modal-backdrop')closeModal()};document.getElementById('modal-enroll').onclick=()=>{db.enrolled=[...new Set([...(db.enrolled||[]),c.id])];if(!isCourseStarted(c.id))db.startedCourses=[...(db.startedCourses||[]),c.id];save();closeModal();openCourse(c.id)}}
function installProfileMenu(){document.addEventListener('click',async event=>{const trigger=event.target.closest('#profile-toggle');if(trigger){const menu=document.getElementById('profile-menu');if(menu){menu.hidden=!menu.hidden;trigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded',String(!menu.hidden))}return}if(event.target.closest('#profile-signout')){const menu=document.getElementById('profile-menu');if(menu)menu.hidden=true;try{await fetch('/api/logout',{method:'POST',credentials:'same-origin'})}catch{}db={...defaults};view='Overview';viewCourse=null;applyTheme();renderLoginPage();return}if(!event.target.closest('.profile-wrap')){const menu=document.getElementById('profile-menu');if(menu&&!menu.hidden){menu.hidden=true;document.getElementById('profile-toggle')?.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false')}}});document.addEventListener('keydown',event=>{if(event.key==='Escape'){const menu=document.getElementById('profile-menu');if(menu&&!menu.hidden){menu.hidden=true;document.getElementById('profile-toggle')?.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false');document.getElementById('profile-toggle')?.focus()}}})}
function installAcademicHandlers(){document.addEventListener('click',event=>{const button=event.target.closest('[data-lesson]');if(!button)return;event.preventDefault();event.stopImmediatePropagation();showLesson(button.dataset.cid,Number(button.dataset.lesson))},true)}
function installPhotoHandlers(){document.addEventListener('change',event=>{if(event.target.id!=='profile-photo-input')return;const file=event.target.files?.[0];if(!file)return;if(!['image/jpeg','image/png','image/webp'].includes(file.type)||file.size>2*1024*1024){toast('Choose a JPEG, PNG or WebP photo under 2 MB.');event.target.value='';return}const reader=new FileReader();reader.onload=async()=>{try{const response=await fetch('/api/profile/photo',{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},credentials:'same-origin',body:JSON.stringify({data:reader.result})}),data=await response.json();if(!response.ok)throw Error(data.error||'Could not save profile photo.');db.hasPhoto=true;go(view);toast('Profile photo saved to your account.')}catch(e){toast(e.message)}};reader.onerror=()=>toast('Could not read that photo.');reader.readAsDataURL(file)});document.addEventListener('click',async event=>{if(!event.target.closest('#remove-profile-photo'))return;try{const response=await fetch('/api/profile/photo',{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},credentials:'same-origin',body:JSON.stringify({remove:true})}),data=await response.json();if(!response.ok)throw Error(data.error||'Could not remove the photo.');db.hasPhoto=false;go(view);toast('Profile photo removed.')}catch(e){toast(e.message)}})}
function rateFlashcard(rating){const card=flashSession[flashIndex];if(!card)return;const stored=db.flashcards.find(x=>x.id===card.id);if(!stored)return;const interval=Number(stored.interval)||0,ease=Number(stored.ease)||2.5;let days;if(rating==='again'){stored.reps=0;stored.ease=Math.max(1.3,ease-.2);days=10/(24*60)}else if(rating==='hard'){stored.reps=(stored.reps||0)+1;stored.ease=Math.max(1.3,ease-.15);days=Math.max(1,interval*1.2)}else if(rating==='easy'){stored.reps=(stored.reps||0)+1;stored.ease=ease+.15;days=interval===0?4:interval===1?8:Math.round(interval*ease*1.3)}else{stored.reps=(stored.reps||0)+1;days=interval===0?1:interval===1?3:Math.round(interval*ease)}stored.interval=days;stored.reviews=(stored.reviews||0)+1;stored.dueAt=new Date(Date.now()+days*86400000).toISOString();db.activity=[...(db.activity||[]),{type:'flashcard',label:`Reviewed a flashcard · ${rating}`,at:new Date().toISOString(),minutes:1}];flashIndex++;flashRevealed=false;save();refreshCurrentPage()}
function installStudyTools(){document.addEventListener('click',event=>{const build=event.target.closest('#flash-build-deck');if(build){const c=allCourses().find(x=>x.id===document.getElementById('flash-course')?.value);if(!c)return;const existing=new Set((db.flashcards||[]).map(x=>x.id));const cards=(c.topics||[]).map((topic,i)=>({id:`lesson-${c.id}-${i}`,course:c.id,question:`Explain: ${topic}`,answer:lessonReading(c,i).split(/\n\n/)[0].slice(0,700),ease:2.5,reps:0,interval:0,reviews:0,dueAt:new Date().toISOString()})).filter(x=>!existing.has(x.id));db.flashcards=[...(db.flashcards||[]),...cards];save();refreshCurrentPage();toast(cards.length?`${cards.length} study cards added.`:'That subject deck is already in your library.');return}if(event.target.closest('#flash-start-review')){flashSession=(db.flashcards||[]).filter(c=>!c.dueAt||Date.parse(c.dueAt)<=Date.now());flashIndex=0;flashRevealed=false;refreshCurrentPage();return}if(event.target.closest('#flash-reveal')){flashRevealed=true;refreshCurrentPage();return}if(event.target.closest('[data-flash-rate]')){rateFlashcard(event.target.closest('[data-flash-rate]').dataset.flashRate);return}if(event.target.closest('#flash-exit')||event.target.closest('#flash-finish')){flashSession=[];flashIndex=0;flashRevealed=false;go('Flashcards');return}const del=event.target.closest('[data-flash-delete]');if(del){db.flashcards=(db.flashcards||[]).filter(c=>c.id!==del.dataset.flashDelete);save();refreshCurrentPage()}});document.addEventListener('submit',event=>{if(event.target.id!=='flash-custom-form')return;event.preventDefault();const question=document.getElementById('flash-question').value.trim(),answer=document.getElementById('flash-answer').value.trim();if(!question||!answer)return;db.flashcards=[...(db.flashcards||[]),{id:crypto.randomUUID(),course:document.getElementById('flash-course').value,question,answer,ease:2.5,reps:0,interval:0,reviews:0,dueAt:new Date().toISOString()}];save();refreshCurrentPage();toast('Flashcard saved.')})}
async function saveAdminCourse(course){const response=await fetch('/api/admin/courses',{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},credentials:'same-origin',body:JSON.stringify(course)}),data=await response.json();if(!response.ok)throw Error(data.error||'Course could not be saved.');await loadCatalog();go('Courses');toast('Course saved for all students.')}
async function editAdminCourse(id){const c=allCourses().find(x=>x.id===id);if(!c)return;const title=prompt('Course title',c.title);if(title===null||!title.trim())return;const category=prompt('Subject area',c.category)||c.category;const description=prompt('Short course description',c.description||'')??c.description;const topics=prompt('Modules, separated by commas',(c.topics||[]).join(', '));if(topics===null)return;try{await saveAdminCourse({...c,title:title.trim(),category,description,topics:topics.split(',').map(x=>x.trim()).filter(Boolean),isCustom:!baseCourses.some(x=>x.id===id)})}catch(e){toast(e.message)}}
function installAdminHandlers(){document.addEventListener('submit',async event=>{if(event.target.id==='admin-course-form'){event.preventDefault();const title=document.getElementById('admin-course-title').value.trim(),id='course-'+Date.now(),topics=document.getElementById('admin-course-topics').value.split(',').map(x=>x.trim()).filter(Boolean);try{await saveAdminCourse({id,title,category:document.getElementById('admin-course-category').value,description:document.getElementById('admin-course-description').value.trim(),topics,level:'Beginner',lessons:topics.length,minutes:Math.max(25,topics.length*25),quiz:courses.find(c=>c.id==='dsa')?.quiz,isCustom:true})}catch(e){toast(e.message)}}if(event.target.id==='admin-password-reset-form'){event.preventDefault();const submit=event.target.querySelector('button');submit.disabled=true;try{const response=await fetch('/api/admin/password-reset',{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},credentials:'same-origin',body:JSON.stringify({email:document.getElementById('reset-admin-email').value.trim(),resetToken:document.getElementById('reset-admin-token').value,newPassword:document.getElementById('reset-admin-password').value})}),data=await response.json();if(!response.ok)throw Error(data.error);window.authError='Admin password reset. Log in with the new password.';renderLoginPage()}catch(e){toast(e.message)}finally{if(submit.isConnected)submit.disabled=false}}});document.addEventListener('click',async event=>{const edit=event.target.closest('[data-admin-course-edit]');if(edit){await editAdminCourse(edit.dataset.adminCourseEdit);return}const del=event.target.closest('[data-admin-course-delete]');if(del){const c=allCourses().find(x=>x.id===del.dataset.adminCourseDelete);if(!c||!confirm(`Remove ${c.title} from the course catalogue? Students will no longer see it.`))return;const response=await fetch('/api/admin/courses/'+encodeURIComponent(c.id),{method:'DELETE',credentials:'same-origin'}),data=await response.json();if(!response.ok)return toast(data.error||'Could not remove course.');await loadCatalog();go('Courses');toast('Course removed from the catalogue.');return}const block=event.target.closest('[data-student-block]');if(block){const blocked=block.dataset.blocked==='true',id=block.dataset.studentBlock;if(!confirm(`${blocked?'Unblock':'Block'} this student account?${blocked?'':' They will be signed out and cannot log in.'}`))return;const response=await fetch(`/api/admin/students/${encodeURIComponent(id)}/block`,{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},credentials:'same-origin',body:JSON.stringify({blocked:!blocked})}),data=await response.json();if(!response.ok)return toast(data.error||'Could not update student account.');await loadStudents();toast(blocked?'Student account unblocked.':'Student blocked and signed out.')}})}
init();

function flashcardsPage(){const total=(db.flashcards||[]).length,due=(db.flashcards||[]).filter(c=>!c.dueAt||Date.parse(c.dueAt)<=Date.now()).length;if(flashSession.length){if(flashIndex>=flashSession.length)return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Review complete 🎉</h1><p>You reviewed ${flashSession.length} cards. Spaced practice helps ideas stick.</p></div><div class="panel"><button class="primary-btn" id="flash-finish">Back to flashcards</button></div>`;const card=flashSession[flashIndex],course=allCourses().find(c=>c.id===card.course);return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Flashcard review</h1><p>${course?esc(course.title):'Personal deck'} · Card ${flashIndex+1} of ${flashSession.length}</p></div><div class="flashcard"><div class="flashcard-label">${flashRevealed?'ANSWER':'ACTIVE RECALL'}</div><div class="flashcard-text">${esc(flashRevealed?card.answer:card.question)}</div>${flashRevealed?`<div class="flash-ratings"><button class="rating-again" data-flash-rate="again">Again <small>10 min</small></button><button data-flash-rate="hard">Hard <small>1 day</small></button><button data-flash-rate="good">Good <small>Next interval</small></button><button data-flash-rate="easy">Easy <small>Long interval</small></button></div>`:`<button class="primary-btn" id="flash-reveal">Show answer</button>`}</div><button class="text-btn" id="flash-exit">← Exit review</button>`}return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Flashcards</h1><p>Active recall with spaced review. Cards stay in your account across sessions.</p></div><div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-top">Cards in your library<span class="stat-icon">▣</span></div><div class="stat-num">${total}</div><div class="stat-foot">Saved to your student account</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-top">Due for review<span class="stat-icon">◷</span></div><div class="stat-num">${due}</div><div class="stat-foot">Review again to strengthen recall</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-top">Cards reviewed<span class="stat-icon">✓</span></div><div class="stat-num">${(db.flashcards||[]).reduce((n,c)=>n+(c.reviews||0),0)}</div><div class="stat-foot">Across your saved cards</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-top">Study streak<span class="stat-icon">✦</span></div><div class="stat-num">${studyStreak()} days</div><div class="stat-foot">Keep your learning routine going</div></div></div><div class="content-grid"><div class="panel"><div class="section-head"><h2>Review schedule</h2><button class="primary-btn" id="flash-start-review" ${due?'':'disabled'}>Review ${due} due cards</button></div><p class="course-meta">Cards rated “Again” return in about ten minutes. Hard, Good and Easy schedule the next review farther apart.</p>${(db.flashcards||[]).slice(0,8).map(c=>`<div class="lesson-row"><div class="lesson-dot">▣</div><div class="lesson-copy"><b>${esc(c.question)}</b><span>${esc(allCourses().find(x=>x.id===c.course)?.title||'Personal card')} · ${c.reviews||0} reviews</span></div><span class="badge">${!c.dueAt||Date.parse(c.dueAt)<=Date.now()?'Due':new Date(c.dueAt).toLocaleDateString()}</span></div>`).join('')||'<div class="empty">No cards yet. Build a deck from any course module or write your own question.</div>'}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Build a subject deck</h3><p class="course-meta">Turn course modules into question-and-answer cards. Choose any course; enrolment is not required.</p><label class="field">Course<select id="flash-course" class="search-input" style="width:100%">${allCourses().map(c=>`<option value="${esc(c.id)}">${esc(c.title)}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><button class="primary-btn" id="flash-build-deck" style="margin-top:12px">Build module cards</button><div class="divider"></div><h3>Create a card</h3><form id="flash-custom-form"><label class="field">Question<input id="flash-question" maxlength="300" required placeholder="Ask yourself a concept question"></label><label class="field">Answer<textarea id="flash-answer" class="search-input" maxlength="2000" required rows="4" placeholder="Write a concise answer"></textarea></label><button class="secondary-btn" style="margin-top:10px">Save flashcard</button></form></div></div>`}
function achievementsPage(){const quizAttempts=Object.values(db.attempts||{}),focusSessions=(db.activity||[]).filter(a=>a.type==='focus').length,flashReviews=(db.flashcards||[]).reduce((n,c)=>n+(c.reviews||0),0),awards=[['🌱','First lesson','Complete a course module',(db.completed||[]).length>=1],['📚','Curious mind','Complete five course modules',(db.completed||[]).length>=5],['✓','Quiz explorer','Take your first course quiz',quizAttempts.length>=1],['🏆','Perfect score','Earn a best score of 5/5',quizAttempts.some(a=>a.best===5)],['🔥','Three-day streak','Study on three consecutive days',studyStreak()>=3],['⏱️','Focus builder','Complete three focus sessions',focusSessions>=3],['✍️','Note maker','Save three course notes',(db.notes||[]).length>=3],['🧠','Recall practice','Review ten flashcards',flashReviews>=10],['🎓','Course finisher','Complete any course',allCourses().some(c=>pct(c)===100)]];const earned=awards.filter(a=>a[3]).length;return `<div class="page-title"><h1>Achievements</h1><p>Milestones from your actual lessons, quizzes and study sessions.</p></div><div class="hero-banner"><div><div class="eyebrow">YOUR PROGRESS</div><h2>${earned} of ${awards.length} milestones earned</h2><p>Achievements are calculated from your saved learning activity.</p></div><button class="primary-btn" data-go="Study planner">Plan a study session →</button></div><div class="achievement-grid">${awards.map(a=>`<article class="achievement-card ${a[3]?'earned':''}"><div class="achievement-icon">${a[3]?a[0]:'🔒'}</div><b>${esc(a[1])}</b><p>${esc(a[2])}</p><span class="badge">${a[3]?'Earned':'In progress'}</span></article>`).join('')}</div>`}
function applyTheme(){document.body.classList.toggle('dark-theme',db.settings?.theme==='dark')}
function applyRolePermissions(){if(db.role==='admin')return;document.getElementById('add-session')?.remove();document.getElementById('new-assignment')?.remove();document.getElementById('add-course')?.remove();document.getElementById('reset-data')?.remove();document.querySelectorAll('[data-admin-course-edit],[data-admin-course-delete],[data-edit]').forEach(el=>el.remove());const name=document.getElementById('setting-name');if(name)name.disabled=true;document.getElementById('save-settings')?.remove()}
function refreshCurrentPage(){const page=document.querySelector('.page');if(page)page.innerHTML=renderView()}
function startFocus(){if(focusRunning)return;focusRunning=true;const chosen=Number(document.getElementById('focus-duration')?.value)||25;if(focusRemaining<=0||focusRemaining===25*60)focusRemaining=chosen*60;focusHandle=setInterval(()=>{focusRemaining--;const clock=document.getElementById('focus-clock');if(clock)clock.textContent=formatClock(focusRemaining);if(focusRemaining<=0){clearInterval(focusHandle);focusHandle=null;focusRunning=false;db.activity=[...(db.activity||[]),{type:'focus',label:'Completed a focus study session',at:new Date().toISOString(),minutes:chosen}];save();toast('Focus session complete. Nice work!');refreshCurrentPage()}else{const button=document.getElementById('focus-toggle');if(button)button.textContent='Pause focus'}},1000);const button=document.getElementById('focus-toggle');if(button)button.textContent='Pause focus'}
function pauseFocus(){focusRunning=false;if(focusHandle){clearInterval(focusHandle);focusHandle=null}const button=document.getElementById('focus-toggle');if(button)button.textContent='Resume focus'}
function installAdvancedHandlers(){document.addEventListener('click',event=>{const theme=event.target.closest('#theme-toggle');if(theme){db.settings={...(db.settings||{}),theme:db.settings?.theme==='dark'?'light':'dark'};applyTheme();theme.textContent=db.settings.theme==='dark'?'☀':'☾';theme.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(db.settings.theme==='dark'));save();return}if(event.target.closest('#focus-toggle')){focusRunning?pauseFocus():startFocus();return}if(event.target.closest('#focus-reset')){pauseFocus();focusRemaining=(Number(document.getElementById('focus-duration')?.value)||25)*60;const clock=document.getElementById('focus-clock');if(clock)clock.textContent=formatClock(focusRemaining);const button=document.getElementById('focus-toggle');if(button)button.textContent='Start focus';return}const del=event.target.closest('[data-task-delete]');if(del){db.planner=(db.planner||[]).filter(t=>t.id!==del.dataset.taskDelete);save();refreshCurrentPage();return}const noteDel=event.target.closest('[data-note-delete]');if(noteDel){db.notes=(db.notes||[]).filter(n=>n.id!==noteDel.dataset.noteDelete);save();refreshCurrentPage();toast('Note deleted.');return}const roadmap=event.target.closest('[data-roadmap-course]');if(roadmap){const id=roadmap.dataset.roadmapCourse;if(!isEnrolled(id)){db.enrolled=[...enrolledIds(),id];save()}viewCourse=id;go('My learning')}});document.addEventListener('change',event=>{const check=event.target.closest('[data-task-done]');if(!check)return;const task=(db.planner||[]).find(t=>t.id===check.dataset.taskDone);if(task){task.done=check.checked;if(task.done)db.activity=[...(db.activity||[]),{type:'planner',label:`Completed study task · ${task.title}`,at:new Date().toISOString(),minutes:1}];save();refreshCurrentPage()}});document.addEventListener('change',event=>{if(event.target.id==='focus-duration'&&!focusRunning){focusRemaining=Number(event.target.value)*60;const clock=document.getElementById('focus-clock');if(clock)clock.textContent=formatClock(focusRemaining)}});document.addEventListener('submit',event=>{if(event.target.id==='planner-form'){event.preventDefault();const title=document.getElementById('task-title').value.trim();if(!title)return;db.planner=[...(db.planner||[]),{id:crypto.randomUUID(),title,course:document.getElementById('task-course').value,date:document.getElementById('task-date').value,minutes:Number(document.getElementById('task-minutes').value),done:false}];save();refreshCurrentPage();toast('Study task added.')}if(event.target.id==='notes-form'){event.preventDefault();const title=document.getElementById('note-title').value.trim(),body=document.getElementById('note-body').value.trim();if(!title||!body)return;db.notes=[...(db.notes||[]),{id:crypto.randomUUID(),course:document.getElementById('note-course').value,title,body,at:new Date().toISOString()}];save();refreshCurrentPage();toast('Note saved to your account.')}})}
